{
  "raw": {
    "https://careers-nyit.icims.com/jobs/4310/director%2c-administration-%26-operations-for-college-of-arts-%26-sciences/job": {
      "title": "Director, Administration & Operations for College of Arts & Sciences",
      "description": "Director, Administration & Operations for College of Arts & Sciences Job Location(s) US-NY-Old Westbury Posted Date 3 days ago (10/16/2026 5:11 PM) Job ID 2026-4766 Division College of Arts & Sciences Position Type Staff Type Regular Full-Time Category Business and Financial Operations Work Mode Hybrid Overview New York Institute of Technology's six schools and colleges offer undergraduate, graduate, doctoral, and professional degree programs in in-demand disciplines including computer science, data science, and cybersecurity; biology, health professions, and medicine; architecture and design; engineering; IT and digital technologies; management; and energy and sustainability. A nonprofit, independent, private, and nonsectarian institute of higher education founded in 1955, it welcomes nearly 8,000 students worldwide. The university has campuses in New York City and Long Island, New York; Jonesboro, Arkansas; and Vancouver, British Columbia, as well as programs around the world. More than 120,000 alumni are part of an engaged network of physicians, architects, scientists, engineers, business leaders, digital artists, and healthcare professionals. Together, the university’s community of doers, makers, healers, and innovators empowers graduates to change the world, solve 21st-century challenges, and reinvent the future. For more information, visit nyit.edu . Reporting to the Dean for the College of Arts & Sciences, the Director of Administration & Operations serves as a strategic partner, providing oversight of administrative operations, budget planning, personnel processes, project management, and key initiatives that advance the college's mission and strategic priorities. As a trusted advisor, this role drives operational excellence, aligns resources and processes with institutional goals, and fosters collaboration across the university community. Responsibilities The Director is the primary budget officer for the college and supports the Dean with fiscal oversight including purchasing, budget planning, forecasting and analysis, financial reconciliation and reporting. Working with the Dean and Departmental Chairs, prepare annual budget submission, including detailed budget proposal, staffing plan, new faculty requests, capital requests, and all supporting analysis. Cost center manager for all CAS departments, approving all budget amendments, reimbursement requests, requisitions, and period activity pay (stipends) in Workday. Prepare allocation schedule of instructional release and approve faculty load management submissions. Review of all grants, external and internal, to determine faculty stipends, release and grant budget required, and incorporate this funding into overall budget plan. Works collaboratively with the Dean’s administrative staff to coordinate the day-to-day activities of the Dean and Associate Dean. Primary liaison to central university budget and finance. Provides financial and resource context for all strategic planning efforts of the college. Ensures that all institutional procedures and policies are adhered to as it relates to purchasing and requisitions, p-card use, staff T&E expenses, reconciliation, and reimbursements. Point person for all operations-related issues, space planning, logistics, and facility maintenance as it relates to all areas used by the college, as well as oversight of all college capital projects. Coordinates all appropriate human resource actions including new hire requests, modification to current staff’s status, position descriptions, and job searches. In-depth knowledge of all financial data systems available at NYIT (i.e., Workday, PeopleSoft, PowerBI) as well as become well-versed in all university policies and procedures related to accounting/fiscal activities and accountability. The Director processes all financial transactions and assists the Dean and senior management in making spending decisions. Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications A Bachelor’s degree in Business Administration, accounting or related field. An MBA is preferred. Must have extensive experience (5 year plus) in a financial services environment or a higher education business office setting. Must have knowledge of budget oversight and planning. Proficiency in Microsoft Office, including Word, Excel, Outlook, PowerPoint, and familiarity with Workday is necessary. Candidate must be able to work effectively and collegially with all levels of management and staff. Successful candidate must have excellent organizational and problem-solving abilities as well as strong interpersonal skills. Excellent customer service skills. Must have the ability to manage all personnel and fiscal matters in a professional and highly confidential manner. Ability to work independently, efficiently, and accurately in stressful situations. Ability to be detail-oriented, thorough, and accurate. Excellent professional communication skills demonstrating consistency and clarity. C ommitment to deadlines, ability to develop and execute work plans and to prioritize and handle multiple assignments from multiple individuals promptly and accurately. Other Information New York Institute of Technology offers numerous opportunities to enhance personal and professional growth and provides employees with a competitive compensation and benefits program inclusive of generous paid time off, holidays, tuition remission, and retirement plans with employer contributions. New York Institute of Technology is an Equal Opportunity Employer – All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. In compliance with local legislation as well as to provide greater transparency to candidates, the annual base salary range for this position is listed. New York Tech considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate experience/expertise, education/training, key skills, geographic location, internal peer equity as well as market, organizational considerations and/or applicable collective bargaining agreement when extending an offer. Minimum Salary USD $120,000.00/Yr. Maximum Salary USD $140,000.00/Yr. Options Create Profile & Apply Apply Share Email this job to a friend Refer Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com"
    },
    "https://careers-nyit.icims.com/jobs/4309/assistant-dean%2c-student-administration/job": {
      "title": "Assistant Dean, Student Administration",
      "description": "Assistant Dean, Student Administration Job Location(s) US-AR-Jonesboro Posted Date 1 week ago (10/9/2026 11:07 PM) Job ID 2026-4758 Division College of Osteopathic Medicine Position Type Staff Type Regular Full-Time Category Student Administration Work Mode Hybrid Overview New York Institute of Technology's six schools and colleges offer undergraduate, graduate, doctoral, and professional degree programs in in-demand disciplines including computer science, data science, and cybersecurity; biology, health professions, and medicine; architecture and design; engineering; IT and digital technologies; management; and energy and sustainability. A nonprofit, independent, private, and nonsectarian institute of higher education founded in 1955, it welcomes nearly 8,000 students worldwide. The university has campuses in New York City and Long Island, New York; Jonesboro, Arkansas; and Vancouver, British Columbia, as well as programs around the world. More than 120,000 alumni are part of an engaged network of physicians, architects, scientists, engineers, business leaders, digital artists, and healthcare professionals. Together, the university’s community of doers, makers, healers, and innovators empowers graduates to change the world, solve 21st-century challenges, and reinvent the future. For more information, visit nyit.edu . Summary: New York Institute of Technology's Jonesboro, Arkansas campus is seeking an Assistant Dean, Student Administration . Reporting to the Campus Dean, the incumbent provides strategic leadership and operational oversight for all Student Administration functions at the Arkansas campus of New York Institute of Technology College of Osteopathic Medicine, including Admissions, Financial Aid, Registrar, Student Life, Career Development, Counseling and Wellness, and Pipeline/Pathway Programs. Responsibilities include implementing institutional policies, supervising key departmental leaders, coordinating major campus events and student success initiatives, managing outreach and post-baccalaureate programs, serving on multiple college committees and the senior management team, overseeing Title IX activities, and ensuring high-quality student services, wellness support, and access to academic and administrative resources for students at the Arkansas location. Responsibilities Serve as a senior advisor to campus leadership and participate as a member of the campus Senior Leadership Team, contributing to institutional planning, policy development, and operational decision-making Provide executive leadership, policies, processes and strategic oversight for all Student Administration functions at the Arkansas campus, including Admissions, Financial Aid, Registrar, Student Life, Career and Residency Placement, Counseling and Wellness, and Pathway Programs Responsible for developing and coordinating all College events including, but not limited to: Orientation, Enrollment Services days, White Coat Ceremony, Match Day Ceremony, and the Graduation/Hooding Ceremony on the campus at A-State in Jonesboro, AR Provide oversight and fiscal management of an approximately $1.15 million annual budget, ensuring responsible allocation of resources, ongoing expenditure monitoring, and alignment with departmental and institutional priorities Coordinate the implementation of the Admissions and Financial Aid policies and procedures with the Central Processing area leaders located in Old Westbury Develop and coordinate college outreach and academic preparation programs to serve as a pipeline for students’ engagement and enrollment Lead the coordination and implementation of the Freshman-to-Physician Pathway Program partnerships, supporting students throughout their undergraduate experience through intentional programming, advising, and experiences designed to prepare them for successful admission to and transition into medical school Serve as a member of the NYITCOM Admissions Oversight Committee, Admissions Decisions Committee, Student Progress Committee, Ethics and Professionalism Board Advisor, and Behavioral Intervention Team Serve as the campus Title IX designee, providing leadership for compliance, training, investigations, prevention efforts, and related policy implementation Lead the development, implementation, and continuous improvement of policies, procedures, and operational processes that support student success, engagement, retention, and overall campus experience Supervise counseling and wellness professionals who lead initiatives and student support services, ensuring access to physical health, mental health, counseling, and other resources that promote student well-being Perform other duties and special projects as assigned Qualifications • Master's Degree required • 5-10 years’ experience in higher education, preferably in admissions, financial aid, recruitment, student life, student conduct • Required to obtain certification as Title IX Investigator • Substantial experience in student services administration • Proven ability to work effectively with a diverse community of students, alumni, faculty and staff • Excellent communications and interpersonal skills • Experience in developing and managing budgets Other Information New York Institute of Technology offers numerous opportunities to enhance personal and professional growth and provides employees with a competitive compensation and benefits program inclusive of generous paid time off, holidays, and retirement plans with employer contributions. New York Institute of Technology is an Equal Opportunity Employer – All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. Options Create Profile & Apply Apply Share Email this job to a friend Refer Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com"
