    "https://careers-nyit.icims.com/jobs/4306/associate-general-counsel-%26-director-of-compliance/job": {
      "title": "Associate General Counsel & Director of Compliance",
      "description": "Associate General Counsel & Director of Compliance Job Location(s) US-NY-Old Westbury Posted Date 4 weeks ago (9/24/2026 9:15 AM) Job ID 2026-4750 Division General Counsel's Office Position Type Staff Type Regular Full-Time Category Legal Work Mode Hybrid Overview New York Institute of Technology's six schools and colleges offer undergraduate, graduate, doctoral, and professional degree programs in in-demand disciplines including computer science, data science, and cybersecurity; biology, health professions, and medicine; architecture and design; engineering; IT and digital technologies; management; and energy and sustainability. A nonprofit, independent, private, and nonsectarian institute of higher education founded in 1955, it welcomes nearly 8,000 students worldwide. The university has campuses in New York City and Long Island, New York; Jonesboro, Arkansas; and Vancouver, British Columbia, as well as programs around the world. More than 120,000 alumni are part of an engaged network of physicians, architects, scientists, engineers, business leaders, digital artists, and healthcare professionals. Together, the university’s community of doers, makers, healers, and innovators empowers graduates to change the world, solve 21st-century challenges, and reinvent the future. For more information, visit nyit.edu . The Office of the General Counsel has three lawyers (General Counsel, Vice President for Human Resources & Secretary; Associate General Counsel & Director of Compliance; and Assistant General Counsel) and a manager of legal operations. The department also works in tandem with the Title IX, Title VI & 504 Coordinator, who works in the Office of Access and Engagement, and is also a lawyer. The Associate General Counsel & Director of Compliance reports to the General Counsel and assists in providing practical, solution-oriented legal advice, analysis, and strategic counsel to all of the university's constituencies, including senior administrators, faculty and staff. Responsibilities Key Responsibilities will include: Working with departments throughout the university, overseeing regulatory compliance at the federal, state and local levels, including, among others, in the areas of financial aid, grants compliance, discrimination, privacy and data security Advising on student matters, including student conduct, disability accommodations, discrimination, academic issues and FERPA Providing commercial transaction support across the institution Specific Responsibilities will include : Keep current on developments in laws and regulations at the federal, state and local level pertaining to higher education institutions. Proactively identify emerging legal and regulatory risks and recommend measures to promote compliance, prevent disputes, mitigate institutional exposure, and avoid litigation. Develop, implement, review, and maintain institutional policies and compliance programs to promote legal compliance and mitigate institutional risk. Provide legal and compliance training to faculty, staff, and administrators as needed. Draft, review, negotiate and strategize on an array of commercial and academic contracts. Training and oversight of contractual and other work of the Assistant General Counsel and manager of legal operations. Represent the General Counsel's Office on institutional committees, working groups, and cross-functional initiatives. Field a wide range of legal inquiries from departments university-wide. Conduct legal research and analysis. Assist outside counsel in litigation activities including document production, as well as reviewing and monitoring written submissions, depositions and trials. Report potential claims and relevant factual circumstances to the appropriate insurance companies. Oversee timely and appropriate responses on behalf of the university to requests for records and other information as required, including, but not limited to, under the Family Educational Rights and Privacy Act (FERPA) and subpoenas Assist with the university’s responses to complaints, subpoenas, citations, reporting obligations, requests for information, and other inquiries or proceedings initiated by governmental or non-governmental organizations. Qualifications Minimum Required Qualifications: • Juris Doctor from ABA-accredited U.S. law school. • Seven (7) years of experience practicing law in a university/college legal department, law firm, or other applicable corporate legal department. Strong preference for candidates who have significant experience with higher education regulatory compliance in either an in-house or law firm setting. • Licensed to practice law in the State of New York in good standing (or ability to obtain licensure promptly after date of hire). Knowledge, Skills and Experience: • Ability to manage a high volume and variety of contracts and other matters from routine to complex and stay organized and accountable • Knowledge and understanding of institutional policies and procedures and the regulatory environment in which they operate • Experience in reviewing, drafting, negotiating, and editing contracts • Strong written and oral communication skills and ability to translate complex legal issues for non-lawyers • Ability to respond quickly and appropriately to emergency situations and to meet deadlines • Ability to analyze situations and identify legal, compliance, and risk issues, propose alternative practical solutions, project consequences of proposed actions, and recommend actions aligned with the school’s mission and goals while addressing stakeholder concerns • Collaborative and flexible approach and ability to work with individuals from a wide range of constituencies in a diverse community • Accuracy and meticulous attention to detail • Excellent critical thinking and listening skills. • Highest level of research and analytical skills. • Sound judgment, impeccable integrity and maintenance of confidentiality Please submit cover letter & resume for consideration. The position can be partially hybrid, with the expectation of being in the office on the Long Island campus in Old Westbury, New York, generally three or four days per week. Other Information New York Institute of Technology offers numerous opportunities to enhance personal and professional growth and provides employees with a competitive compensation and benefits program inclusive of generous paid time off, holidays, tuition remission, and retirement plans with employer contributions. New York Institute of Technology is an Equal Opportunity Employer – All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. In compliance with local legislation as well as to provide greater transparency to candidates, the annual base salary range for this position is listed. New York Tech considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate experience/expertise, education/training, key skills, geographic location, internal peer equity as well as market, organizational considerations and/or applicable collective bargaining agreement when extending an offer. Minimum Salary USD $175,000.00/Yr. Maximum Salary USD $200,000.00/Yr. Options Create Profile & Apply Apply Share Email this job to a friend Refer Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com"
    },
    "https://careers-nyit.icims.com/jobs/4304/catalog-%26-metadata-librarian-librarian-i/job": {
      "title": "Catalog & Metadata Librarian-Librarian I",
      "description": "Catalog & Metadata Librarian-Librarian I Job Location(s) US-NY-Old Westbury Posted Date 4 weeks ago (9/24/2026 2:12 PM) Job ID 2026-4748 Division Library Position Type Staff Type Regular Full-Time Category Library Overview New York Institute of Technology's six schools and colleges offer undergraduate, graduate, doctoral, and professional degree programs in in-demand disciplines including computer science, data science, and cybersecurity; biology, health professions, and medicine; architecture and design; engineering; IT and digital technologies; management; and energy and sustainability. A nonprofit, independent, private, and nonsectarian institute of higher education founded in 1955, it welcomes nearly 8,000 students worldwide. The university has campuses in New York City and Long Island, New York; Jonesboro, Arkansas; and Vancouver, British Columbia, as well as programs around the world. More than 120,000 alumni are part of an engaged network of physicians, architects, scientists, engineers, business leaders, digital artists, and healthcare professionals. Together, the university’s community of doers, makers, healers, and innovators empowers graduates to change the world, solve 21st-century challenges, and reinvent the future. For more information, visit nyit.edu . Responsibilities New York Institute of Technology’s Old Westbury campus seeks a Catalog & Metadata Librarian. The Catalog & Metadata Librarian is responsible for the creation, maintenance, and quality control of bibliographic records and metadata for New York Tech Libraries’ print, electronic, and digital resources. The position ensures that library resources are accurately described, organized, discoverable, and accessible through the library’s integrated library system, discovery services, and other resource platforms. The Catalog Librarian works collaboratively with public services, acquisitions, electronic resources, and other library staff to support effective resource discovery and access. The position also contributes to the development and implementation of cataloging and metadata standards, policies, workflows, and procedures and stays current with emerging practices and technologies in library metadata and resource description. Responsibilities: Provide original and copy catalog services for monographs, serials, electronic resources, theses, tech items, video and other library materials using current national and international cataloging standards. Create accurate, standards-based bibliographic records that improve the discovery, identification, organization, and accessibility of information resources. Apply appropriate classification, subject headings, descriptive metadata, and access points to support resource discovery. Conduct ongoing database maintenance, including identifying and correcting duplicate, incomplete, inaccurate, or inconsistent bibliographic records. Manage and maintain catalog records for electronic resources and other online materials, ensuring accurate links and access information. Work with acquisitions and electronic resources staff to ensure that newly acquired materials are accurately represented and discoverable in the library catalog and discovery system. Troubleshoot cataloging and metadata-related problems and respond to questions from library staff regarding bibliographic records and resource discovery. Provide support for the institutional repository. Participate in university and library committees, professional development activities, and institutional initiatives as assigned. Perform other duties related to library technical services and resource discovery as assigned. Qualifications Master’s degree in Library Information Science from an ALA accredited institution required. 1-3 years of relevant academic library experience. Knowledge of current cataloging and metadata standards and practices. Demonstrated knowledge of MARC21, RDA, Library of Congress Classification, and Library of Congress Subject Headings. Experience with an integrated library system and library discovery platform. Preferred experience with OCLC and WorldCat. Strong attention to detail and ability to maintain accuracy while managing multiple priorities. Excellent analytical, organizational, communication, and problem-solving skills. Ability to work independently as well as collaboratively with colleagues across the library. Other Information New York Institute of Technology offers numerous opportunities to enhance personal and professional growth and provides employees with a competitive compensation and benefits program inclusive of generous paid time off, holidays, tuition remission, and retirement plans with employer contributions. New York Institute of Technology is an Equal Opportunity Employer – All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. In compliance with local legislation as well as to provide greater transparency to candidates, the annual base salary range for this position is listed. New York Tech considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate experience/expertise, education/training, key skills, geographic location, internal peer equity as well as market, organizational considerations and/or applicable collective bargaining agreement when extending an offer. Minimum Salary USD $70,000.00/Yr. Maximum Salary USD $75,000.00/Yr. Options Create Profile & Apply Apply Share Email this job to a friend Refer Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com"
    },
    "https://careers-nyit.icims.com/jobs/4303/assistant-associate-professor-nursing%2c-tenure---track/job": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor Nursing, Tenure - Track",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor Nursing, Tenure - Track Job Location(s) US-NY-Old Westbury Posted Date 4 weeks ago (9/23/2026 2:18 PM) Job ID 2026-4747 Division School of Health Professions Position Type Faculty Type Regular Full-Time Category School of Health Professions Overview New York Institute of Technology's six schools and colleges offer undergraduate, graduate, doctoral, and professional degree programs in in-demand disciplines including computer science, data science, and cybersecurity; biology, health professions, and medicine; architecture and design; engineering; IT and digital technologies; management; and energy and sustainability. A nonprofit, independent, private, and nonsectarian institute of higher education founded in 1955, it welcomes nearly 8,000 students worldwide. The university has campuses in New York City and Long Island, New York; Jonesboro, Arkansas; and Vancouver, British Columbia, as well as programs around the world. More than 120,000 alumni are part of an engaged network of physicians, architects, scientists, engineers, business leaders, digital artists, and healthcare professionals. Together, the university’s community of doers, makers, healers, and innovators empowers graduates to change the world, solve 21st-century challenges, and reinvent the future. For more information, visit nyit.edu . NYIT’s School of Health Professions, Department of Nursing is seeking faculty to fill a full-time tenure track position located at the Old Westbury campus. Responsibilities Assist in the day-to-day operations of the Department of Nursing. Participate, and demonstrate leadership, in the implementation, and evaluation of a competency-based curriculum and other nursing education program components. Assist students toward successful program completion. Participate in activities that promote the stature of the department. Develop and maintain ongoing relationships within the community, including fostering the nursing education program’s responsiveness to community/employer needs. Ensures overall integrity/quality in the delivery of the nursing program. Ensure the curricular assessment data is used to recommend quality enhancements to teaching styles and curricular content specific to nursing. Identify factors in the nursing curriculum that warrant further evaluation and/or assessment using benchmark data. Enforce and monitor procedures and programs that demonstrate commitment to an inclusive environment within the Department of Nursing. Qualifications Must hold a doctoral degree, Ph.D., Ed.D., or DNP Must have an established research agenda. Knowledge/practice experience of Medical/Surgical nursing, Pharmacology, and Foundations of nursing. Experience with simulation in nursing. Position will require the candidate to coordinate all simulation activities and work towards SSH’s accreditation for Healthcare Simulation Programs. Experience with curriculum development. Experience writing NCLEX style questions. Hold a New York State unencumbered RN license. Minimum of 3 years’ experience teaching at the collegiate level. Certified Nurse Educator certification a plus. Have knowledge of CCNE standards and essentials. Other Information New York Institute of Technology offers numerous opportunities to enhance personal and professional growth and provides employees with a competitive compensation and benefits program inclusive of generous paid time off, holidays, tuition remission, and retirement plans with employer contributions. New York Institute of Technology is an Equal Opportunity Employer – All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. In compliance with local legislation as well as to provide greater transparency to candidates, the annual base salary range for this position is listed. New York Tech considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate experience/expertise, education/training, key skills, geographic location, internal peer equity as well as market, organizational considerations and/or applicable collective bargaining agreement when extending an offer. Minimum Salary USD $110,000.00/Yr. Maximum Salary USD $120,000.00/Yr. Options Create Profile & Apply Apply Share Email this job to a friend Refer Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com"
    },
    "https://careers-nyit.icims.com/jobs/4302/research-technician/job": {
      "title": "Research Technician",
      "description": "Research Technician Job Location(s) US-AR-Jonesboro Posted Date 4 weeks ago (9/24/2026 11:47 AM) Job ID 2026-4745 Division College of Osteopathic Medicine Position Type Staff Type Regular Full-Time Category Research Overview New York Institute of Technology's six schools and colleges offer undergraduate, graduate, doctoral, and professional degree programs in in-demand disciplines including computer science, data science, and cybersecurity; biology, health professions, and medicine; architecture and design; engineering; IT and digital technologies; management; and energy and sustainability. A nonprofit, independent, private, and nonsectarian institute of higher education founded in 1955, it welcomes nearly 8,000 students worldwide. The university has campuses in New York City and Long Island, New York; Jonesboro, Arkansas; and Vancouver, British Columbia, as well as programs around the world. More than 120,000 alumni are part of an engaged network of physicians, architects, scientists, engineers, business leaders, digital artists, and healthcare professionals. Together, the university’s community of doers, makers, healers, and innovators empowers graduates to change the world, solve 21st-century challenges, and reinvent the future. For more information, visit nyit.edu . The New York Institute of Technology's College of Osteopathic Medicine seeks a Research Technician located at the Jonesboro, Arkansas campus. The ideal Research Technician candidate would have experience with fundamental cellular and molecular biology techniques, as well as experience working with research animals. This is a grant approved role and is subject to the duration of the grant. Responsibilities Small animal handling and in vivo studies. Laboratory organization and purchasing. Experiments related to cellular and molecular biology. Data collection, analysis, and maintenance of records. General laboratory maintenance. Research project assistance. Qualifications High school diploma A bachelor’s degree (e.g., B.S., B.A.) in Biology, Chemistry, Physiology, Biochemistry, or related fields. Experience related to handling laboratory equipment is preferred. Experience related to handling laboratory equipment. Experience with molecular biological techniques such as Electrophoresis, Polymerase Chain Reaction (PCR), etc., is preferred Experience working with basic science laboratory equipment and with laboratory research animals and cell culture is preferred. Strong work ethic and an interest in developing independent research projects are preferred. Must have excellent oral and written communication and interpersonal skills Other Information New York Institute of Technology offers numerous opportunities to enhance personal and professional growth and provides employees with a competitive compensation and benefits program inclusive of generous paid time off, holidays, and retirement plans with employer contributions. New York Institute of Technology is an Equal Opportunity Employer – All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. Options Create Profile & Apply Apply Share Email this job to a friend Refer Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com"
