    "https://careers-nyit.icims.com/jobs/4301/groundsperson/job": {
      "title": "Groundsperson",
      "description": "Groundsperson Job Location(s) US-NY-Old Westbury Posted Date 2 weeks ago (10/8/2026 1:07 PM) Job ID 2026-4742 Division Facilities Position Type Staff Type Regular Full-Time Category Building and Grounds Cleaning and Maintenance Overview New York Institute of Technology's six schools and colleges offer undergraduate, graduate, doctoral, and professional degree programs in in-demand disciplines including computer science, data science, and cybersecurity; biology, health professions, and medicine; architecture and design; engineering; IT and digital technologies; management; and energy and sustainability. A nonprofit, independent, private, and nonsectarian institute of higher education founded in 1955, it welcomes nearly 8,000 students worldwide. The university has campuses in New York City and Long Island, New York; Jonesboro, Arkansas; and Vancouver, British Columbia, as well as programs around the world. More than 120,000 alumni are part of an engaged network of physicians, architects, scientists, engineers, business leaders, digital artists, and healthcare professionals. Together, the university’s community of doers, makers, healers, and innovators empowers graduates to change the world, solve 21st-century challenges, and reinvent the future. For more information, visit nyit.edu . Responsibilities New York Tech’s Long Island campus seeks a Groundsperson to work Monday – Friday, 10:00AM – 6:30 PM. The Groundsperson title is in the Collective Bargaining Agreement with Local 282. The Groundsperson performs routine manual labor to maintain campus grounds, including landscape cleaning and seasonal outdoor maintenance. The role requires regular physical activity and the use of hand and power tools. Essential Job Functions Perform lawn care, including mowing, trimming, edging, and blowing debris Remove trash, leaves, and debris from grounds, walkways, and parking areas Perform snow and ice removal, including shoveling, salting, and operating snow equipment Operate equipment such as lawn mowers, trimmers, leaf blowers, and small machinery Load, unload, and transport materials such as soil, mulch, tools, and equipment Identify and report unsafe conditions or maintenance issues Perform general outdoor maintenance as assigned Physical Demands Frequent standing, walking, bending, kneeling, and reaching Ability to lift, carry, push, and pull up to 50 lbs. regularly Use of hands for gripping, handling, and operating tools and equipment Repetitive motions including bending and twisting Ability to work outdoors in varying weather conditions (heat, cold, rain, snow) Work Environment Outdoor work in all seasons and weather conditions Exposure to noise, dust, pollen, and equipment fumes Use of personal protective equipment (PPE) as required Qualifications Previous landscaping, outdoor maintenance, and snow plowing experience preferred. HS Diploma or equivalent. Must be computer literate. Must have a valid NYS driver’s license. Ability to work unsupervised on assigned tasks. Other Information New York Institute of Technology offers numerous opportunities to enhance personal and professional growth and provides employees with a competitive compensation and benefits program inclusive of generous paid time off, holidays, tuition remission, and retirement plans with employer contributions. New York Institute of Technology is an Equal Opportunity Employer – All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. In compliance with local legislation as well as to provide greater transparency to candidates, the annual base salary range for this position is listed. New York Tech considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate experience/expertise, education/training, key skills, geographic location, internal peer equity as well as market, organizational considerations and/or applicable collective bargaining agreement when extending an offer. Minimum Salary USD $43.53/Hr. Maximum Salary USD $43.53/Hr. Options Create Profile & Apply Apply Share Email this job to a friend Refer Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com"
    },
    "https://careers-nyit.icims.com/jobs/4300/office-assistant/job": {
      "title": "Office Assistant",
      "description": "Office Assistant Job Location(s) US-NY-Central Islip Posted Date 3 weeks ago (10/1/2026 11:43 AM) Job ID 2026-4738 Division College of Osteopathic Medicine Position Type Staff Type Regular Full-Time Category College of Osteopathic Medicine Overview New York Institute of Technology's six schools and colleges offer undergraduate, graduate, doctoral, and professional degree programs in in-demand disciplines including computer science, data science, and cybersecurity; biology, health professions, and medicine; architecture and design; engineering; IT and digital technologies; management; and energy and sustainability. A nonprofit, independent, private, and nonsectarian institute of higher education founded in 1955, it welcomes nearly 8,000 students worldwide. The university has campuses in New York City and Long Island, New York; Jonesboro, Arkansas; and Vancouver, British Columbia, as well as programs around the world. More than 120,000 alumni are part of an engaged network of physicians, architects, scientists, engineers, business leaders, digital artists, and healthcare professionals. Together, the university’s community of doers, makers, healers, and innovators empowers graduates to change the world, solve 21st-century challenges, and reinvent the future. For more information, visit nyit.edu . Responsibilities New York Institute of Technology's College of Osteopathic Medicine Family Health Care Center is seeking a full-time Office Assistant for our clinic in Central Islip. We are seeking a highly organized and personable Office Assistant to join our clinic. In this role, you will be the first point of contact for patients, providing exceptional customer service while handling administrative tasks efficiently. The ideal candidate will have strong communication skills, attention to detail, and the ability to manage multiple responsibilities in a fast-paced environment. Key Responsibilities: Oversee the process of physician orders which may require approval/authorization from insurance companies and/or third-party vendor portals. Obtains information necessary to complete the prior authorization for radiology, medication, and/or other medical services. (Includes collecting all the necessary documentation, contacting the ordering physician for additional information or asking questions regarding the order, and determining from a quick overview whether the order is likely to be approved (prior-auth) and is ready to be moved on to prior-authorization stage.) Answer telephone, take all incoming messages and appropriately document in the electronic medical record. Handle all appointment scheduling. Greet and receive patients ensuring a welcoming and postiive experience and obtain appropriate patient and financial information. Document patient arrival, verify patient information and obtain appropriate consents and signatures. Process patient payments, including co-pays and past due balances, and handle billing inquiries. Assist with patient referrals, ensuring necessary documentation is sent to the appropriate medical facilities. Follow up with specialists to collect visit summary notes. Coordinate communication between patients, doctors, billing and other clinic staff. Log patient communication in eClinicalWorks (eCW) via telephone encounters. Maintain a clean and organized front desk and waiting area. Managed electronic health records (EHR) and ensure patient confidentiality in accordance with HIPAA regulations. Other duties as assigned. Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent required. Preferred Medical Assistant Training and/or certification. Prior experience with patient scheduling or working in a medical health center preferred. Familiarity with Medical Terminology. Computer skills (use of an electronic medical record system required). Operating knowledge of personal computers and MS Windows applications (including Word, Excel and Outlook) Strong communication skills, both verbal and written. Ability to work with sensitive and confidential information and adheres to AHC HIPAA Compliance Program. Strong organizational skills and attention to detail. Maintain an approachable demeanor with a focus on patient care. Must be able to interact with patients, insurers and team members in a responsible, professional and ethical manner. Ability to self-motivate. Bi-lingual Spanish preferred. Other Information New York Institute of Technology offers numerous opportunities to enhance personal and professional growth and provides employees with a competitive compensation and benefits program inclusive of generous paid time off, holidays, tuition remission, and retirement plans with employer contributions. New York Institute of Technology is an Equal Opportunity Employer – All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. In compliance with local legislation as well as to provide greater transparency to candidates, the annual base salary range for this position is listed. New York Tech considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate experience/expertise, education/training, key skills, geographic location, internal peer equity as well as market, organizational considerations and/or applicable collective bargaining agreement when extending an offer. Minimum Salary USD $35,000.00/Yr. Maximum Salary USD $38,000.00/Yr. Options Create Profile & Apply Apply Share Email this job to a friend Refer Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com"
    },
    "https://careers-nyit.icims.com/jobs/4299/administrative-assistant/job": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant",
      "description": "Administrative Assistant Job Location(s) US-AR-Jonesboro Posted Date 4 weeks ago (9/22/2026 2:34 PM) Job ID 2026-4669 Division College of Osteopathic Medicine Position Type Staff Type Regular Full-Time Category Administrative/Clerical Overview New York Institute of Technology's six schools and colleges offer undergraduate, graduate, doctoral, and professional degree programs in in-demand disciplines including computer science, data science, and cybersecurity; biology, health professions, and medicine; architecture and design; engineering; IT and digital technologies; management; and energy and sustainability. A nonprofit, independent, private, and nonsectarian institute of higher education founded in 1955, it welcomes nearly 8,000 students worldwide. The university has campuses in New York City and Long Island, New York; Jonesboro, Arkansas; and Vancouver, British Columbia, as well as programs around the world. More than 120,000 alumni are part of an engaged network of physicians, architects, scientists, engineers, business leaders, digital artists, and healthcare professionals. Together, the university’s community of doers, makers, healers, and innovators empowers graduates to change the world, solve 21st-century challenges, and reinvent the future. For more information, visit nyit.edu . The New York Institute of Technology's Jonesboro, Arkansas campus is seeking an Administrative Assistant to support the Department of Clinical Medicine. Reporting directly to the Chair of Clinical Medicine, the Administrative Assistant will provide comprehensive administrative support and assist with the day-to-day operations of the department. Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Responsibilities Greet students, visitors, and guests to the department. Originates written materials, transcribing dictation. Schedules and coordinating calendar and special events. Maintains files and databases. Keeps inventory of department supplies. Originates purchases and processing invoices for the department and faculty. Monitors and assist with department budget. Assists with projects. Answers questions, resolve problems as they arise. Takes meeting minutes Maintains information for department and/or school. Processes forms, Liaison between students and faculty Assists with Lab attendance. General administrative duties assigned by supervisor. Qualifications High school diploma required plus 2-3 years of administrative/clerical support experience required OR Associates degree or higher preferred plus 1-2 years of administrative/clerical support experience required in a professional office. Excellent interpersonal skills, good computer skills, and solid administrative/organizational skills. Ability to work independently and have good judgement. Proficiency in Microsoft Office. Strong computer skills with the ability to organize virtual meetings, use of Zoom, Teams. Ability to quickly learn new systems/software packages. Other Information New York Institute of Technology offers numerous opportunities to enhance personal and professional growth and provides employees with a competitive compensation and benefits program inclusive of generous paid time off, holidays, and retirement plans with employer contributions. New York Institute of Technology is an Equal Opportunity Employer – All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. Options Create Profile & Apply Apply Share Email this job to a friend Refer Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com"
    },
    "https://careers-nyit.icims.com/jobs/4298/associate-bursar/job": {
      "title": "Associate Bursar",
      "description": "Associate Bursar Job Location(s) US-NY-Old Westbury Posted Date 1 month ago (9/17/2026 3:37 PM) Job ID 2026-4735 Division Enrollment Services Position Type Staff Type Regular Full-Time Category Bursar and Student Accounts Overview New York Institute of Technology's six schools and colleges offer undergraduate, graduate, doctoral, and professional degree programs in in-demand disciplines including computer science, data science, and cybersecurity; biology, health professions, and medicine; architecture and design; engineering; IT and digital technologies; management; and energy and sustainability. A nonprofit, independent, private, and nonsectarian institute of higher education founded in 1955, it welcomes nearly 8,000 students worldwide. The university has campuses in New York City and Long Island, New York; Jonesboro, Arkansas; and Vancouver, British Columbia, as well as programs around the world. More than 120,000 alumni are part of an engaged network of physicians, architects, scientists, engineers, business leaders, digital artists, and healthcare professionals. Together, the university’s community of doers, makers, healers, and innovators empowers graduates to change the world, solve 21st-century challenges, and reinvent the future. For more information, visit nyit.edu . New York Institute of Technology seeks an Associate Bursar located at the Old Westbury campus. New York Institute of Technology seeks an Associate Bursar to support the administration and collection of student accounts, payment processing, and account reconciliation. This position is responsible for reviewing student tuition and fee accounts, communicating with students regarding outstanding balances and payment obligations, and implementing strategies to reduce delinquency, financial risk, and institutional liability. The Associate Bursar provides comprehensive customer service and account support to students at the Old Westbury location, including students affiliated with New York Tech, NYITCOM, and Global campuses. The position works closely with campus partners to ensure student accounts are accurate, payments and financial aid are properly applied, and account issues are resolved in a timely manner. Responsibilities Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Provide professional, responsive, and solution-oriented customer service to students regarding billing, payments, account balances, and financial obligations. Make and receive telephone calls and respond to student inquiries through email and other communication channels. Review student accounts to ensure all eligible financial aid has been properly awarded, posted, and applied. Monitor and review payment plans, communicate upcoming payment deadlines, and send reminders regarding payments due. Respond to inquiries related to account balances, late payment fees, payment plans, due dates, refunds, and other billing matters. Collaborate with the Registrar, Financial Aid, Academic Departments, and other campus partners to resolve issues involving grades, withdrawals, enrollment dates, registration changes, and other matters that may affect student account balances. Follow up on account corrections, adjustments, credits, and other transactions to ensure they are processed accurately and in a timely manner. Monitor student accounts for accuracy of charges, payments, financial aid, coding, and other account activity. Work closely with the Registrar, Collections, Security, Library, Financial Aid, Counseling & Wellness, Housing, Admissions, and other departments to support timely and accurate cohort and student account processing. Assist management with student communication initiatives, including text, email, and telephone campaigns related to payments, balances, deadlines, and delinquent accounts. Support Bursar operations at the New York City campus, as needed, including orientation, open house, graduation, and other special events, as well as coverage during staff absences and high-volume registration periods. Reconcile daily banking and payment reports and collaborate closely with the Accounting Office to ensure accurate financial reporting and transaction processing. Assist with internal and external audits, system testing, process improvements, and implementation of system or policy changes. Maintain compliance with applicable federal and New York State laws, regulations, institutional policies, and financial aid and student account requirements Apply knowledge of collections practices, compliance requirements, and account receivables processes to support effective delinquency management. Monitor delinquent accounts and take appropriate action to reduce outstanding balances and prevent past-due accounts from progressing to default. Maintain confidentiality and safeguard sensitive student and financial information in accordance with institutional policies and applicable regulations. Perform other duties and special projects assigned by Bursar management. Qualifications A bachelor’s degree is required; a master’s degree is preferred. Collections, banking, or university experience is preferred. Excellent communication skills, including clear and strong written and verbal skills and strong attention to detail is required. Knowledge of Microsoft Office and ability to work independently and collaboratively. Student Accounts or Financial Aid, Accounting, Banking or Collection experience preferred. Proficient in Microsoft Office, PeopleSoft experience preferred. Excellent customer service experience is required. Strong attention to detail, organizational and analytical skills are required. This position can spend time based at either the NYC or Long Island campuses and may be eligible for some remote work inline with NY Tech policy. This position may require some night and/or holiday/weekend hours. Other Information New York Institute of Technology offers numerous opportunities to enhance personal and professional growth and provides employees with a competitive compensation and benefits program inclusive of generous paid time off, holidays, tuition remission, and retirement plans with employer contributions. New York Institute of Technology is an Equal Opportunity Employer – All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. In compliance with local legislation as well as to provide greater transparency to candidates, the annual base salary range for this position is listed. New York Tech considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate experience/expertise, education/training, key skills, geographic location, internal peer equity as well as market, organizational considerations and/or applicable collective bargaining agreement when extending an offer. Minimum Salary USD $58,000.00/Yr. Maximum Salary USD $60,000.00/Yr. Options Create Profile & Apply Apply Share Email this job to a friend Refer Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com"
    },
    "https://careers-nyit.icims.com/jobs/4297/mechanic-a---electrician/job": {
      "title": "Mechanic A - Electrician",
      "description": "Mechanic A - Electrician Job Location(s) US-NY-Old Westbury Posted Date 3 weeks ago (9/29/2026 3:24 PM) Job ID 2026-4643 Division Facilities Operations Position Type Staff Type Regular Full-Time Category Facilities Management Overview New York Institute of Technology's six schools and colleges offer undergraduate, graduate, doctoral, and professional degree programs in in-demand disciplines including computer science, data science, and cybersecurity; biology, health professions, and medicine; architecture and design; engineering; IT and digital technologies; management; and energy and sustainability. A nonprofit, independent, private, and nonsectarian institute of higher education founded in 1955, it welcomes nearly 8,000 students worldwide. The university has campuses in New York City and Long Island, New York; Jonesboro, Arkansas; and Vancouver, British Columbia, as well as programs around the world. More than 120,000 alumni are part of an engaged network of physicians, architects, scientists, engineers, business leaders, digital artists, and healthcare professionals. Together, the university’s community of doers, makers, healers, and innovators empowers graduates to change the world, solve 21st-century challenges, and reinvent the future. For more information, visit nyit.edu . Responsibilities New York Tech’s Long Island campus seeks a Mechanic A - Electrician to work Monday – Friday, 7am – 3:30 pm. The Mechanic A title is in the Collective Bargaining Agreement with Local 282. The Mechanic A will report to the General Foreman and Management on the status of operation, repair and maintenance and preventive maintenance of campus equipment as assigned. Mechanic A will be responsible for scheduling repairs and maintenance around occupancy of campus facilities with emphasis on safety and code compliance. The Mechanic A is responsible for maintaining inventory and sourcing needs including tools and equipment. You will be expected to operate motor vehicles to perform duties efficiently and must have and maintain a valid and appropriate NYS Driver's License. Mechanic A will have specialized skills in electrical systems (line voltage and low voltage systems), including but not limited to fire alarm and BMS systems. Mechanic A is expected to perform work at journeyman level in electrical assignments as well as skilled to semi-skilled level of work in combination of other trades (including but not limited to plumbing, HVAC, snow removal, etc.) Mechanic A can be assigned tasks in specializations other than these as directed and in line with the collective bargaining agreement. Requirements: Ability to read blueprints and schematic drawings Extensive experience in troubleshooting equipment to identify faults Ability to perform medium to heavy physical labor Ability to work unsupervised on assigned tasks Qualifications Minimum four years of full-time experience in a trade under a skilled journeyman mechanic which provided training equivalent to that given in an apprentice program. HS Diploma or equivalent and/or trade school certification. Must be computer literate. Must have a valid NYS driver license. Other Information New York Institute of Technology offers numerous opportunities to enhance personal and professional growth and provides employees with a competitive compensation and benefits program inclusive of generous paid time off, holidays, tuition remission, and retirement plans with employer contributions. New York Institute of Technology is an Equal Opportunity Employer – All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. In compliance with local legislation as well as to provide greater transparency to candidates, the annual base salary range for this position is listed. New York Tech considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate experience/expertise, education/training, key skills, geographic location, internal peer equity as well as market, organizational considerations and/or applicable collective bargaining agreement when extending an offer. Minimum Salary USD $53.89/Hr. Maximum Salary USD $53.89/Hr. Options Create Profile & Apply Apply Share Email this job to a friend Refer Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com"
