    "https://careers-nyit.icims.com/jobs/4296/systems-engineer/job": {
      "title": "Systems Engineer",
      "description": "Systems Engineer Job Location(s) US-NY-Old Westbury Posted Date 1 month ago (9/15/2026 2:57 PM) Job ID 2026-4728 Division Networks, Systems & Telecommunications. Position Type Staff Type Regular Full-Time Category Information Technology Overview New York Institute of Technology's six schools and colleges offer undergraduate, graduate, doctoral, and professional degree programs in in-demand disciplines including computer science, data science, and cybersecurity; biology, health professions, and medicine; architecture and design; engineering; IT and digital technologies; management; and energy and sustainability. A nonprofit, independent, private, and nonsectarian institute of higher education founded in 1955, it welcomes nearly 8,000 students worldwide. The university has campuses in New York City and Long Island, New York; Jonesboro, Arkansas; and Vancouver, British Columbia, as well as programs around the world. More than 120,000 alumni are part of an engaged network of physicians, architects, scientists, engineers, business leaders, digital artists, and healthcare professionals. Together, the university’s community of doers, makers, healers, and innovators empowers graduates to change the world, solve 21st-century challenges, and reinvent the future. For more information, visit nyit.edu . NYIT seeks a Systems Engineer, to be located at the Old Westbury campus. The position can be considered for a hybrid/remote position with flexibility of working remotely and in our NYC or Old Westbury offices as in line with New York Tech remote work policy. The Systems Engineer is a trusted resource who will work collaboratively with NYIT’s IT infrastructure and Information Security team to design, configure, troubleshoot, and maintain NYIT’s systems infrastructure ensuring the availability of production and test systems. The Systems Engineer serves as a senior technical resource responsible for managing complex server environments, authentication systems, Microsoft 365 services, automation platforms, and research computing infrastructure while providing advanced technical support for faculty, staff, students, and administrative departments. This position will contribute to the efforts of safeguarding the confidentiality, integrity, and availability of the enterprise infrastructure across the university. The incumbent will be required to participate in Systems related workgroups, to cross train members of the systems team and develop support runbooks. The successful incumbent will possess outstanding communication skills while adhering to our high standard of excellence. They will be team players with the ability to work independently and possess strong analytical and multitasking skills. This position plays a critical role in ensuring stability, security, availability, and performance of institutional technology systems that support the University's academic, research, and administrative missions. Responsibilities Administer/Manage the existing Microsoft, Linux, VDI, Backup, Cloud and Systems Infrastructure, provide suggestions on continuous improvements and iterations. Administer/Manage Microsoft Hyper-V virtualization infrastructure, including deployment, configuration, performance monitoring, lifecycle management, and patching. Administer/Manage and maintain Active Directory and Microsoft Entra ID identity platforms. Administer/Manage Microsoft 365 environment including Exchange Online, Teams, ands SharePoint. Administer/Manage Linux-based systems supporting High-Performance Computing (HPC) and research initiatives. Monitor and improve the lifecycle of services from inception and design, through deployment, operation and refinement. Provide hands-on development and oversight of the software development lifecycle of the automation tools used by the IT infrastructure team. Assists in performing hardware implementations, ensure configuration, process, and procedural standards are followed. Support print management infrastructure, including PaperCut print services. Direct the automation and orchestration of workloads across on-prem and cloud providers. Collaborate with Information Technology team members to develop secure system automation and monitoring systems. Assist in Incident response and information security investigations. Provide second and third level support for troubleshooting of systems infrastructure and performance issues. Research, analyze, and recommend changes for future system growth by utilizing industry standard monitoring and research tools for core infrastructure solutions. Assist in the design, implementation and maintenance of NYIT’s storage and backup solution. Maintain a patching credence for all systems. Mentor colleagues and staff members in usage and administration of existing and new cloud and infrastructure technologies. Development of configuration, process, and procedure standards. Create, maintain and enforce SLAs. Qualifications BS in computer science, engineering, or other technical discipline. Experience in a higher education environment is preferred. Minimum of 5 recent years’ systems engineering experience including management and technology experience with enterprise-level systems, cloud-based services, and endpoint infrastructure support; experience providing IT support in an academic environment preferred. UNIX/Linux/Microsoft on-prem and cloud system administration experience required, applicable industry certification(s) are desired. Experience with High-Performance Computing and Linux Administration. Windows system administration experience, including Active Directory, Office365 and TEAMS is desired. Hands-on experience with UNIX/Linux/Windows system and program installation, compilation and configuration as well as enterprise endpoint management tools such as SCCM and JAMF. Working knowledge of databases, SQL and the application of continuous integration (CI) and continuous deployment solutions. Proficient with concepts of a wide range of tools and technologies in Infrastructure management, deployment and development. Experience with at least one scripting language, such as Python, Perl, Bash, or PowerShell. Knowledge of cybersecurity best practices and regulatory compliance requirements Functional knowledge of standards-based networking applications. Functional knowledge of account management processes, directory and authentication services (LDAP), as well as DNS, DHCP, HTTP, NFS, SAMBA, CAS, ADFS, SAML, etc. Demonstrated passion for problem solving; strong project management skills and the proven ability to build trust and work well with all levels of management and technical staff are required. Able to communicate effectively with people at varying levels of technical fluency including the ability to explain and document complex technical issues in a way that non-technical and/or inexperienced people may understand; the ability to establish collaborative working relationships at all contact levels of the University; the ability to communicate progress/challenges to appropriate personnel effectively. Must possess strong analytical skills as well as active listening skills and a high degree of integrity relative to computer security and confidentiality of information. Ability to work independently and as part of a team; ability to work concurrently on multiple tasks and projects. Team player with excellent consulting skills and a fun, but professional presence required. Excellent customer service skills; a high degree of integrity relative to data security and confidentiality of information required. Ability to work nights and weekends on an as-needed basis is required. Other Information New York Institute of Technology offers numerous opportunities to enhance personal and professional growth and provides employees with a competitive compensation and benefits program inclusive of generous paid time off, holidays, tuition remission, and retirement plans with employer contributions. New York Institute of Technology is an Equal Opportunity Employer – All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. In compliance with local legislation as well as to provide greater transparency to candidates, the annual base salary range for this position is listed. New York Tech considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate experience/expertise, education/training, key skills, geographic location, internal peer equity as well as market, organizational considerations and/or applicable collective bargaining agreement when extending an offer. Minimum Salary USD $115,000.00/Yr. Maximum Salary USD $130,000.00/Yr. Options Create Profile & Apply Apply Share Email this job to a friend Refer Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com"
    },
    "https://careers-nyit.icims.com/jobs/4295/special-projects-and-acquisitions-library-associate/job": {
      "title": "Special Projects and Acquisitions Library Associate",
      "description": "Special Projects and Acquisitions Library Associate Job Location(s) US-NY-Old Westbury Posted Date 1 month ago (9/10/2026 3:42 PM) Job ID 2026-4732 Division Library Position Type Staff Type Regular Full-Time Category Education, Training, and Library Occupations Overview New York Institute of Technology's six schools and colleges offer undergraduate, graduate, doctoral, and professional degree programs in in-demand disciplines including computer science, data science, and cybersecurity; biology, health professions, and medicine; architecture and design; engineering; IT and digital technologies; management; and energy and sustainability. A nonprofit, independent, private, and nonsectarian institute of higher education founded in 1955, it welcomes nearly 8,000 students worldwide. The university has campuses in New York City and Long Island, New York; Jonesboro, Arkansas; and Vancouver, British Columbia, as well as programs around the world. More than 120,000 alumni are part of an engaged network of physicians, architects, scientists, engineers, business leaders, digital artists, and healthcare professionals. Together, the university’s community of doers, makers, healers, and innovators empowers graduates to change the world, solve 21st-century challenges, and reinvent the future. For more information, visit nyit.edu . Responsibilities The Special Projects and Acquisitions Library Associate supports various tasks related to special projects, including assistance with assessments, grants, annual reports, and other strategic initiatives. This role also supports the acquisition of library materials for the New York Tech Libraries. The Library Associate works with vendors, processes orders, verifies invoices, and tracks budget expenditures. Key Responsibilities: Assist with planning, organizing, and executing special projects, including assessments, grants, and annual reports. Acquire all print books, e-books, media, streaming videos, and rush reserve titles for all NYIT libraries (excluding NYITCOM). Order, receive, and verify resources to prevent duplication. Process payments for all materials ordered and received. Order books and e-books through YBP/GOBI. Order supplies for all three NYIT libraries. Trace missing, backordered, or incorrect orders as needed, and arrange for credits or returns. Maintain and track book budget expenditures for the three NYIT libraries. Process orders and payments using Workday platform and institutional credit cards. Maintain budgetary spreadsheets for various vendors to ensure accurate allocation and tracking of funds. Generate reports for books ordered and received, outstanding/back-ordered titles, and special reports required by national/state organizations (e.g., ACRL) and for accreditation purposes. Maintain statistics on database expenditures, monthly and yearly fiscal data, and ongoing tracking of new titles ordered by library and/or HEGIS code. Perform fiscal year-end closeout tasks, including closing orders and rolling them over into the new fiscal year. Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications Bachelor Degree required. Strong organizational and problem-solving skills, with excellent attention to detail. Ability to prepare and maintain accurate and timely reports. Effective at managing multiple projects and tasks simultaneously. Strong analytical, written, and verbal communication skills. Proficiency in Microsoft Office, especially Microsoft Excel, library management systems. Ability to communicate effectively with vendors and colleagues. Other Information New York Institute of Technology offers numerous opportunities to enhance personal and professional growth and provides employees with a competitive compensation and benefits program inclusive of generous paid time off, holidays, tuition remission, and retirement plans with employer contributions. New York Institute of Technology is an Equal Opportunity Employer – All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. In compliance with local legislation as well as to provide greater transparency to candidates, the annual base salary range for this position is listed. New York Tech considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate experience/expertise, education/training, key skills, geographic location, internal peer equity as well as market, organizational considerations and/or applicable collective bargaining agreement when extending an offer. Minimum Salary USD $49,000.00/Yr. Maximum Salary USD $49,000.00/Yr. Options Create Profile & Apply Apply Share Email this job to a friend Refer Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com"
    },
    "https://careers-nyit.icims.com/jobs/4294/instruction-%26-scholarly-communications-librarian-i/job": {
      "title": "Instruction & Scholarly Communications Librarian I",
      "description": "Instruction & Scholarly Communications Librarian I Job Location(s) US-NY-Old Westbury Posted Date 1 month ago (9/10/2026 3:42 PM) Job ID 2026-4725 Division Library Position Type Staff Type Regular Full-Time Category Education, Training, and Library Occupations Overview New York Institute of Technology's six schools and colleges offer undergraduate, graduate, doctoral, and professional degree programs in in-demand disciplines including computer science, data science, and cybersecurity; biology, health professions, and medicine; architecture and design; engineering; IT and digital technologies; management; and energy and sustainability. A nonprofit, independent, private, and nonsectarian institute of higher education founded in 1955, it welcomes nearly 8,000 students worldwide. The university has campuses in New York City and Long Island, New York; Jonesboro, Arkansas; and Vancouver, British Columbia, as well as programs around the world. More than 120,000 alumni are part of an engaged network of physicians, architects, scientists, engineers, business leaders, digital artists, and healthcare professionals. Together, the university’s community of doers, makers, healers, and innovators empowers graduates to change the world, solve 21st-century challenges, and reinvent the future. For more information, visit nyit.edu . Responsibilities New York Institute of Technology’s Old Westbury campus seeks an Instruction & Scholarly Communications Librarian I for a newly revised position. The Librarian I will develop and promote scholarly communication services and initiatives and provide instruction, reference assistance, guidance, and support to students and faculty in effectively accessing and using information resources. This position reports to the Director of Public & Technical Services. Responsibilities include: • Provide information literacy instruction based on pedagogy and best practices in information literacy. • Create tutorials, assessment and content for the library website as well as maintain/troubleshoot these learning tools. • Develop marketing and outreach initiatives that promote scholarly communication services. • Serve as the embedded librarian for undergraduate programs, providing research consultations, course-integrated instruction, and tailored support. • Contribute to the development, management, and promotion of the university's institutional repository. • Provide research consultations to users both in person and virtually. • Deliver workshops for faculty and students on scholarly communication topics, including open access, author rights, open educational resources, and research metrics. • Contribute to collection development by identifying and selecting relevant resources based on user needs and emerging trends. • Serve as liaison to academic departments and research units as assigned. • Participate in library & college committee responsibilities. Qualifications Master’s degree in library/information science from an ALA accredited institution. 1-3 years of relevant academic library experience. Excellent communication skills, both oral and written, with the ability to foster positive working relationships and build partnerships. Demonstrated ability to work independently and collaboratively. Effective time, organizational, and project management skills. Experience providing research support, instruction or consultation services. Knowledge of scholarly publishing, copyright, open access and scholarly communication issues in higher education. Demonstrates an understanding of issues and trends in reference and information literacy. Stays abreast of emerging trends and technologies in the field of library and information science. Demonstrated commitment to diversity, equity, inclusion, accessibility, and user-centered service. Other Information New York Institute of Technology offers numerous opportunities to enhance personal and professional growth and provides employees with a competitive compensation and benefits program inclusive of generous paid time off, holidays, tuition remission, and retirement plans with employer contributions. New York Institute of Technology is an Equal Opportunity Employer – All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. In compliance with local legislation as well as to provide greater transparency to candidates, the annual base salary range for this position is listed. New York Tech considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate experience/expertise, education/training, key skills, geographic location, internal peer equity as well as market, organizational considerations and/or applicable collective bargaining agreement when extending an offer. Minimum Salary USD $61,500.00/Yr. Maximum Salary USD $61,500.00/Yr. Options Create Profile & Apply Apply Share Email this job to a friend Refer Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com"
    },
    "https://careers-nyit.icims.com/jobs/4293/adjunct-faculty--electrical-%26-computer-engineering/job": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty- Electrical & Computer Engineering",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty- Electrical & Computer Engineering Job Location(s) US-NY-Old Westbury Posted Date 1 month ago (9/8/2026 5:22 PM) Job ID 2026-4714 Division College of Engineering & Computing Sciences Position Type Adjunct Type Adjunct Category College of Engineering and Computing Sciences Overview New York Institute of Technology's six schools and colleges offer undergraduate, graduate, doctoral, and professional degree programs in in-demand disciplines including computer science, data science, and cybersecurity; biology, health professions, and medicine; architecture and design; engineering; IT and digital technologies; management; and energy and sustainability. A nonprofit, independent, private, and nonsectarian institute of higher education founded in 1955, it welcomes nearly 8,000 students worldwide. The university has campuses in New York City and Long Island, New York; Jonesboro, Arkansas; and Vancouver, British Columbia, as well as programs around the world. More than 120,000 alumni are part of an engaged network of physicians, architects, scientists, engineers, business leaders, digital artists, and healthcare professionals. Together, the university’s community of doers, makers, healers, and innovators empowers graduates to change the world, solve 21st-century challenges, and reinvent the future. For more information, visit nyit.edu . Responsibilities The Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering at New York Institute of Technology, Long Island, is looking for an Adjunct Faculty to teach Electrical and Computer Engineering and an introductory course for all Engineering undergraduate students at its Old Westbury campus. Qualifications Candidates should have a M.S. or Ph.D. degree in Electrical and Computer Engineering or a related area. Teaching experience or industrial experience in Electrical and Computer Engineering and related Lab applications are preferred. Other Information New York Institute of Technology is an Equal Opportunity Employer – All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. In compliance with local legislation as well as to provide greater transparency to candidates, the annual base salary range for this position is listed. New York Tech considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate experience/expertise, education/training, key skills, geographic location, internal peer equity as well as market, organizational considerations and/or applicable collective bargaining agreement when extending an offer. Adjunct Faculty offered hourly rate is contingent on applicable rank. Minimum Salary USD $101.00/Hr. Maximum Salary USD $110.00/Hr. Options Create Profile & Apply Apply Share Email this job to a friend Refer Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com"
