    "https://careers-nyit.icims.com/jobs/4290/director-of-medical-library/job": {
      "title": "Director of Medical Library",
      "description": "Director of Medical Library Job Location(s) US-NY-Old Westbury Posted Date 1 month ago (9/18/2026 2:50 PM) Job ID 2026-4718 Division College of Osteopathic Medicine Position Type Staff Type Regular Full-Time Category Library Work Mode Onsite Overview New York Institute of Technology's six schools and colleges offer undergraduate, graduate, doctoral, and professional degree programs in in-demand disciplines including computer science, data science, and cybersecurity; biology, health professions, and medicine; architecture and design; engineering; IT and digital technologies; management; and energy and sustainability. A nonprofit, independent, private, and nonsectarian institute of higher education founded in 1955, it welcomes nearly 8,000 students worldwide. The university has campuses in New York City and Long Island, New York; Jonesboro, Arkansas; and Vancouver, British Columbia, as well as programs around the world. More than 120,000 alumni are part of an engaged network of physicians, architects, scientists, engineers, business leaders, digital artists, and healthcare professionals. Together, the university’s community of doers, makers, healers, and innovators empowers graduates to change the world, solve 21st-century challenges, and reinvent the future. For more information, visit nyit.edu . Responsibilities New York Institute of Technology- College of Osteopathic Medicine (COM) seeks a Director of Medical Library at our Long Island (Old Westbury) campus. Reporting to the Associate Dean, the candidate will oversee the New York Based COM library team. Responsibilities include: Work closely with the library team and the medical library at the Jonesboro, AR campus to establish programs, services and activities that meet the instructional, research and clinical needs of the department/school. Support faculty, researchers and students engaged in data intensive research, including assistance with data discovery, management, and the use of relevant tools and methodologies, working collaboratively with the libraries team. Serve as a liaison to departments within the COM and to the School of Health Professions, providing outreach, instruction, collection support and research consultation services. Design and teach instruction sessions in a variety of formats to meet the needs of diverse user groups. This may include the creation of asynchronous learning tools/objects. Coordinate a systematic review service, help researchers and students navigate systematic reviews from protocol to publication and conduct systematic review searches. Responsible for the cataloging and classification of library materials in all physical formats and subjects using national standards and local practices (OCLC). Support Docline and OCLC resource sharing processes. Support emerging uses of AI in research and teaching by providing guidance on tools, evaluation of outputs and responsive use, working collaboratively with data and technology teams. Collaborate on evaluating new resources and information platforms. This is an evening position. Hours are Monday - Friday, from 11am - 7pm Qualifications Required Degree(s): M.L.S. or advanced degree with a combination of education and experience commensurate with the requirements of this position. Preferred Degree(s): M.L.S. - Required Field of Expertise: library science; information services. Preferred Field of Expertise: library science; information services Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: - A minimum of five years of experience working in a health science library or academic library providing information services to clinicians. Supervisory experience preferred. Knowledge of cataloging and OCLC preferred; familiarity with the latest library technology preferred. Demonstrated proficiency with emerging learning and research technologies, as well as information retrieval. Knowledge of PubMed, CINAHL and other health sciences databases and demonstrated experience developing search strategies for literature reviews. Ability to work independently and as part of a team in a rapidly changing environment; ability to manage multiple projects and priorities effectively. Demonstrated commitment to lifelong learning and professional growth, with the ability to adapt to evolving technologies, instructional methods and information resources. Other Information New York Institute of Technology offers numerous opportunities to enhance personal and professional growth and provides employees with a competitive compensation and benefits program inclusive of generous paid time off, holidays, tuition remission, and retirement plans with employer contributions. New York Institute of Technology is an Equal Opportunity Employer – All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. In compliance with local legislation as well as to provide greater transparency to candidates, the annual base salary range for this position is listed. New York Tech considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate experience/expertise, education/training, key skills, geographic location, internal peer equity as well as market, organizational considerations and/or applicable collective bargaining agreement when extending an offer. Minimum Salary USD $100,000.00/Yr. Maximum Salary USD $120,000.00/Yr. Options Create Profile & Apply Apply Share Email this job to a friend Refer Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com"
    },
    "https://careers-nyit.icims.com/jobs/4288/associate-provost%2c-academic-and-faculty-excellence/job": {
      "title": "Associate Provost, Academic and Faculty Excellence",
      "description": "Associate Provost, Academic and Faculty Excellence Job Location(s) US-NY-Old Westbury Posted Date 2 months ago (8/25/2026 12:02 PM) Job ID 2026-4695 Division Academic Affairs Position Type Staff Type Regular Full-Time Category Academic Affairs Work Mode Hybrid Overview New York Institute of Technology's six schools and colleges offer undergraduate, graduate, doctoral, and professional degree programs in in-demand disciplines including computer science, data science, and cybersecurity; biology, health professions, and medicine; architecture and design; engineering; IT and digital technologies; management; and energy and sustainability. A nonprofit, independent, private, and nonsectarian institute of higher education founded in 1955, it welcomes nearly 8,000 students worldwide. The university has campuses in New York City and Long Island, New York; Jonesboro, Arkansas; and Vancouver, British Columbia, as well as programs around the world. More than 120,000 alumni are part of an engaged network of physicians, architects, scientists, engineers, business leaders, digital artists, and healthcare professionals. Together, the university’s community of doers, makers, healers, and innovators empowers graduates to change the world, solve 21st-century challenges, and reinvent the future. For more information, visit nyit.edu . Overview: Reporting to the Provost and Executive Vice President and working in partnership with senior university leaders, deans, department chairs, and the Faculty Senate, the Associate Provost, Academic and Faculty Excellence provides leadership for academic quality, curriculum, and academic policy. The Associate Provost also provides leadership for the Center for Faculty Excellence, designing programming that advances instructional quality, curricular innovation, scholarly productivity, and inclusive pedagogy for full-time and adjunct faculty. The incumbent also serves as Acting Provost in times of need. Responsibilities Academic Excellence: Serve as a resource to deans and department chairs on the interpretation and application of faculty policy; Manage faculty workload policy, course releases, and overload processes in partnership with deans and the Office of the Provost; Administer faculty awards, recognition programs, and internal grant competitions, convening and supporting independent selection committees; Serve as a point of contact for faculty questions about academic policy and process, directing grievances, appeals, and complaints arising from personnel decisions to Human Resources, the bargaining unit, or the designated appeal body; Chair the General Education and Curriculum Committees of the Academic Senate, as the Provost’s designee; Liaise with the Libraries, Information Technology Systems, Student Engagement and Development, and other units on matters involving academic concerns; Represent the Office of the Provost on university committees, task forces, and governance bodies as assigned; Serve as Acting Provost as needed. Faculty Excellence: Lead and set the strategic direction of the Center for Faculty Excellence, aligning its programming with the university's academic priorities and with documented faculty needs Lead, supervise, and develop Center staff Design and deliver a comprehensive program of faculty development — e.g., workshops, institutes, communities of practice, faculty development days, consultations, and course design support — for full-time, part-time, and adjunct faculty across all schools and colleges Design and administer new faculty onboarding and multi-year orientation, and coordinate university-wide faculty mentoring efforts Provide confidential, formative consultation on teaching, including classroom observation, course design review, and midterm student feedback Advance evidence-based, inclusive, and learner-centered teaching practice, and support faculty engagement with emerging instructional technologies, including the responsible use of artificial intelligence in teaching and learning Support faculty research and scholarly development, including writing programs, grant-seeking support, and the scholarship of teaching and learning Provide support for portfolio preparation to faculty approaching reappointment, promotion, or tenure through a combination of workshops, exemplar review, narrative development, and individual consultation on documenting teaching, scholarship, and service Partner with the Libraries, Information Technology Servies, Student Engagement and Development, and others to deliver coherent, non-duplicative support to faculty Establish and report on measures of the Center's reach, quality, and impact; use assessment findings to refine programming Manage the Center's budget and resources; pursue external funding where appropriate When available, represent the university in regional and national educational development networks and communities of practice Qualifications Doctorate or terminal degree A record of teaching, scholarship, and service sufficient to warrant appointment, with tenure, at the rank of associate professor or professor at New York Institute of Technology Successful and demonstrated experience with faculty development (e.g., designing and delivering faculty development programming) Knowledge and experience with policy, curriculum, and contracts Demonstrated ability to work well with and earn the trust of both faculty and administrators Working knowledge of faculty personnel processes, including reappointment, promotion, and tenure review Working knowledge of evidence-based pedagogy, inclusive teaching practice, and course design Excellent written and oral communication skills, including the ability to write clearly about policy and to facilitate effectively across disciplines Sound judgment and discretion in handling sensitive and confidential matters Preferred Qualifications : A record of teaching, scholarship, and service sufficient to warrant appointment, with tenure, at the rank of professor at New York Institute of Technology Experience working within a collective bargaining environment Minimum of five years of progressively responsible academic leadership experience — for example, as a department chair, associate dean, center director, or comparable role Experience at a university with professional and technical programs, multiple campuses, and a substantial graduate and international student population Familiarity with regional and specialized accreditation requirements as they pertain to faculty qualifications and credentialing Experience supporting online, hybrid, and technology-enhanced instruction Experience with budget management and staff supervision Other Information New York Institute of Technology offers numerous opportunities to enhance personal and professional growth and provides employees with a competitive compensation and benefits program inclusive of generous paid time off, holidays, tuition remission, and retirement plans with employer contributions. New York Institute of Technology is an Equal Opportunity Employer – All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. In compliance with local legislation as well as to provide greater transparency to candidates, the annual base salary range for this position is listed. New York Tech considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate experience/expertise, education/training, key skills, geographic location, internal peer equity as well as market, organizational considerations and/or applicable collective bargaining agreement when extending an offer. Minimum Salary USD $170,000.00/Yr. Maximum Salary USD $200,000.00/Yr. Options Create Profile & Apply Apply Share Email this job to a friend Refer Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com"
    },
    "https://careers-nyit.icims.com/jobs/4287/medical-assistant/job": {
      "title": "Medical Assistant",
      "description": "Medical Assistant Job Location(s) US-NY-Old Westbury Posted Date 2 months ago (8/26/2026 1:14 PM) Job ID 2026-4687 Division Academic Health Care Center Position Type Staff Type Regular Full-Time Category College of Osteopathic Medicine Overview New York Institute of Technology's six schools and colleges offer undergraduate, graduate, doctoral, and professional degree programs in in-demand disciplines including computer science, data science, and cybersecurity; biology, health professions, and medicine; architecture and design; engineering; IT and digital technologies; management; and energy and sustainability. A nonprofit, independent, private, and nonsectarian institute of higher education founded in 1955, it welcomes nearly 8,000 students worldwide. The university has campuses in New York City and Long Island, New York; Jonesboro, Arkansas; and Vancouver, British Columbia, as well as programs around the world. More than 120,000 alumni are part of an engaged network of physicians, architects, scientists, engineers, business leaders, digital artists, and healthcare professionals. Together, the university’s community of doers, makers, healers, and innovators empowers graduates to change the world, solve 21st-century challenges, and reinvent the future. For more information, visit nyit.edu . NYTech’s College of Osteopathic Medicine seeks a Medical Assistant located at the Old Westbury campus. Responsibilities Verify patient information by interviewing patients, recording medical history, confirming purpose of visit. Prepare patients for examinations by administering preliminary physical tests, taking vital signs and reporting patient history summary. Performs phlebotomy procedures, toxicology exams and EKG's. Review and processes lab requisitions and results within the electronic medical record. Ensure reports and all test results have been received prior to patient’s arrival. (i.e.: .outside labs, diagnostic tests; consult reports, etc.). Ensures abnormal test results, including critical and high priority, are assigned to ordering/covering provider as per policies. Keeps equipment operating by following operating instructions; troubleshooting breakdowns, maintaining supplies, performing preventive maintenance. Secures patient information and maintains patient confidentiality by completing and safeguarding medical records. Maintains safe, secure and healthy work environment by following standards and procedures; complying with OSHA regulations. Adhere to AHC HIPAA Compliance Program. Keeps supplies ready by maintaining inventory of stock, placing orders and verifying receipt. Works collaboratively with practice physicians to ensure efficient medical record documentation through use of EMR. Greet and receive patients. Obtain appropriate patient financial information. Collect payments and print receipt for patients, reconcile cash drawer and at the end of the day print days sheet. Appointment scheduling. Document patient arrival, verify patient information and obtain appropriate consents and signatures. Obtain insurance referral as needed. Check patient Insurance eligibility as needed. Answer telephone, take incoming messages and appropriately document in the electronic medical record. Scan correspondence, reports, etc., in patient’s medical record and assign to appropriate Provider for review. Print medical records upon request upon receipt of an appropriately completed release of record form. Performs other duties as assigned. Qualifications Training/Certificate – Medical Assistant Certificate CPR Certification Knowledge of blood test procedures; triage procedures, lab reports, and medical terminology. Skill in venipuncture procedure, vital signs, operation of EKG’s, medical equipment. Knowledge of electronic medical records. Ability to prepare patients for medical examinations and procedures. Other Information New York Institute of Technology offers numerous opportunities to enhance personal and professional growth and provides employees with a competitive compensation and benefits program inclusive of generous paid time off, holidays, tuition remission, and retirement plans with employer contributions. New York Institute of Technology is an Equal Opportunity Employer – All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. In compliance with local legislation as well as to provide greater transparency to candidates, the annual base salary range for this position is listed. New York Tech considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate experience/expertise, education/training, key skills, geographic location, internal peer equity as well as market, organizational considerations and/or applicable collective bargaining agreement when extending an offer. Minimum Salary USD $35,000.00/Yr. Maximum Salary USD $40,000.00/Yr. Options Create Profile & Apply Apply Share Email this job to a friend Refer Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com"
    },
    "https://careers-nyit.icims.com/jobs/4286/catering-operations-%26-client-service-manager/job": {
      "title": "Catering Operations & Client Service Manager",
      "description": "Catering Operations & Client Service Manager Job Location(s) US-NY-Old Westbury Posted Date 2 months ago (8/24/2026 8:32 AM) Job ID 2026-4691 Division Campus Dining Position Type Staff Type Regular Full-Time Category Food Services Overview New York Institute of Technology's six schools and colleges offer undergraduate, graduate, doctoral, and professional degree programs in in-demand disciplines including computer science, data science, and cybersecurity; biology, health professions, and medicine; architecture and design; engineering; IT and digital technologies; management; and energy and sustainability. A nonprofit, independent, private, and nonsectarian institute of higher education founded in 1955, it welcomes nearly 8,000 students worldwide. The university has campuses in New York City and Long Island, New York; Jonesboro, Arkansas; and Vancouver, British Columbia, as well as programs around the world. More than 120,000 alumni are part of an engaged network of physicians, architects, scientists, engineers, business leaders, digital artists, and healthcare professionals. Together, the university’s community of doers, makers, healers, and innovators empowers graduates to change the world, solve 21st-century challenges, and reinvent the future. For more information, visit nyit.edu . Responsibilities Provide support to dining operations in one or more of the following areas: Create new business and generate new sales within the campus for Catering and Executive Services. Interact daily with customers by initiating contact, planning and following up with contracts/service agreements. Plan, develop, and implement a comprehensive catering and executive program to ensure overall consistency and high quality across the various operations. Provide and ensure highest level of quality and service for the community, executives, conferences, and other VIP's and other customers. Develop training programs for employees and serve as a resource for operations managers to promote quality services. Make periodic and regular on site inspections of assigned units to observe quality of service; food appearance; merchandising and cleanliness and sanitation of areas, equipment, and employee appearance. Resolve customer issues and questions on site. Interact with managers/supervisors, chefs and catering operation supervisor on food set-ups and displays, ensuring the highest quality of food production, standards, presentations, and techniques. Train, schedule, and supervise all catering drivers. Conduct disciplinary actions as needed. Work with publications and advertising to create and plan marketing strategies for areas of responsibility and ensure that these plans are implemented according to the established timelines. Plan special events and theme parties. Respond directly to inquiries and resolve problems based on knowledge of the organization and of the supervisor's preferences. Answer all catering inquiries and compose and drafts forms, reports, or correspondence for the customer/client review and signature. Respond promptly to inquiries, comments, and requests. Rent equipment as needed. Manage staff and coordinate daily schedule, making adjustments and finding alternatives when scheduling problems occur based on knowledge of program requirements and staff availability. Responsible for hands-on service work as needed. Manage Administrative Assistant with all duties and responsibilities in regards to catertrax, purchase orders, catering orders, signage and other duties as assigned Adhere to department purchasing policies; responsible for food and supply purchasing as directed. Maintain the highest levels of sanitation and cleanliness. Prepare payroll, invoices, inventory, labor, and other like reports. Creates and maintains statistical records. Format and prepare complex documents which require the use of specialized software. Assist the assistant director in developing new campus business opportunities. Assist the director in other duties as needed/required. Must be able to work in other areas on campus as needed, such as DeSeversky Mansion, all campus cafes, kiosks, food trucks, and any/all special events on or off campus. Must be able to work in other positions, such as utility, server, attendant/cashier, driver as needed should employees in those positions not be able to work due to vacation, sick or personal time. Must be able to work a flexible schedule including weekends, nights and holidays, as needed All staff are required to have their temperature taken at Main Gate upon entrance to NYIT campus. Face masks will be given to all staff. Face masks are required to be worn as part of the uniform and it is the responsibility of each staff member to launder their mask. Required to follow NYS Mandate as it pertains to PPE, Sanitation and Social Distancing Other duties as assigned. Qualifications Degree in hotel and restaurant management or a recognized culinary institution or equivalent combination and experience. Previous catering and high-end banquet service experience required. Familiarity with Caterease or similar catering database system preferred. Familiarity with POS systems. Advanced knowledge of Excel, PowerPoint, and Word. Excellent oral and written communication skills. Ability to work flexible and demanding hours, including nights, holidays, and weekends when needed. Demonstrated ability and skills with supervision of entry level staff required. Other Information New York Institute of Technology offers numerous opportunities to enhance personal and professional growth and provides employees with a competitive compensation and benefits program inclusive of generous paid time off, holidays, tuition remission, and retirement plans with employer contributions. New York Institute of Technology is an Equal Opportunity Employer – All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. In compliance with local legislation as well as to provide greater transparency to candidates, the annual base salary range for this position is listed. New York Tech considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate experience/expertise, education/training, key skills, geographic location, internal peer equity as well as market, organizational considerations and/or applicable collective bargaining agreement when extending an offer. Minimum Salary USD $75,000.00/Yr. Maximum Salary USD $80,000.00/Yr. Options Create Profile & Apply Apply Share Email this job to a friend Refer Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com"
    },
    "https://careers-nyit.icims.com/jobs/4285/director%2c-admissions/job": {
      "title": "Director, Admissions",
      "description": "Director, Admissions Job Location(s) US-NY-Old Westbury Posted Date 2 months ago (8/28/2026 11:51 AM) Job ID 2026-4681 Division College of Osteopathic Medicine Position Type Staff Type Regular Full-Time Category Student Services Administration Work Mode Onsite Overview New York Institute of Technology's six schools and colleges offer undergraduate, graduate, doctoral, and professional degree programs in in-demand disciplines including computer science, data science, and cybersecurity; biology, health professions, and medicine; architecture and design; engineering; IT and digital technologies; management; and energy and sustainability. A nonprofit, independent, private, and nonsectarian institute of higher education founded in 1955, it welcomes nearly 8,000 students worldwide. The university has campuses in New York City and Long Island, New York; Jonesboro, Arkansas; and Vancouver, British Columbia, as well as programs around the world. More than 120,000 alumni are part of an engaged network of physicians, architects, scientists, engineers, business leaders, digital artists, and healthcare professionals. Together, the university’s community of doers, makers, healers, and innovators empowers graduates to change the world, solve 21st-century challenges, and reinvent the future. For more information, visit nyit.edu . Responsibilities Reporting to the Associate Dean of Student Administration, the Director, Admissions leads all recruitment, admissions, and enrollment activities for the College of Osteopathic Medicine. The Director develops and implements admissions strategies that support enrollment goals to identify, attract, and enroll highly qualified students who align with the College's mission and commitment to excellence while ensuring compliance with accreditation requirements and institutional standards. Responsibilities: Direct/Manage the NYIT College of Osteopathic Medicine Central Admissions Department for two campuses in New York and Arkansas. Develop and oversee implementation of the policies and procedures, oversee personnel, and develop/manage the annual budget. Direct the total enrollment process of NYITCOM New York and Arkansas coordinating with the Admissions Committee to issue acceptances for both campuses. Direct total enrollment process of Émigré Physicians Program (EPP). Maintain statistical reports to enhance recruitment strategies, forecasting, yield management and operational efficiency. Direct/Manage the NYITCOM application process. Upgrade technological processes utilized in the application process. Create an efficient management of applicant data reporting, interview scheduling, student correspondence for both campuses in New York and Arkansas and EPP Program. Direct/Manage the medical school applicant interview process. Chair the faculty interview committee. Create an effective candidate interview process that presents a very positive view of the college by incorporating presentations, faculty interactions, campus tours, and student ambassadors. Develop and implement a marketing plan with the purpose of promoting visibility to generate an annually increasing pool of qualified and diverse applicants. Oversee Long Island on-campus recruitment programming, including Information Sessions/Campus Tours. Establish and maintain partnerships and collaborations with key outside constituents that greatly improve the school's visibility (Pre-Professional Health Advisors, American Association of Colleges of Osteopathic Medicine). Continuously evaluate and restructure the admissions internal operations to substantially improve the workflow and effectiveness of a high volume, fast paced process coordinating all activities between New York and Arkansas. Continually evaluate and upgrade the overall physical set up of the admissions offices in both locations to improve the COM image for students during visitations and interview process. Lead the admissions effort in restructuring special programs to improve student and program quality (BS/DO, Émigré Physicians Program). Create regional recruitment programs which specifically target these populations and develop electronic admissions processes as needed. Create admissions processes for new master’s degrees and other special programs. Collaborate in the creation and implementation of numerous Articulation Agreements for New York and Arkansas. Direct the team to develop and execute all department communication and promotional materials with applicants coordinating efforts with the NYIT Strategic Communication and External Marketing Serve as a key member of the AACOM Council of Osteopathic Medicine Admissions Officers Chair the campus-based admissions decision committees, serve on the medical school central admissions committee and the central enrollment services committee and central student administration management team. Participate in planning of student events (Orientation, Hooding, White Coat Ceremony, and others). Other duties as assigned. Qualifications Required degree: Master’s degree Required Field of Expertise: Admissions, College Administration Knowledge and experience with professional school admissions. Knowledge of admissions recruitment planning. Knowledge of admissions process, educational systems, and requirements for internationally trained students. Effectively manage staff and high-volume process at a multi campus college . Work collaboratively with administrators, faculty, alumni, and outside constituents. Work independently, effectively, and accurately. Strong decision making and problem-solving skills. Other Information New York Institute of Technology offers numerous opportunities to enhance personal and professional growth and provides employees with a competitive compensation and benefits program inclusive of generous paid time off, holidays, tuition remission, and retirement plans with employer contributions. New York Institute of Technology is an Equal Opportunity Employer – All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. In compliance with local legislation as well as to provide greater transparency to candidates, the annual base salary range for this position is listed. New York Tech considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate experience/expertise, education/training, key skills, geographic location, internal peer equity as well as market, organizational considerations and/or applicable collective bargaining agreement when extending an offer. Minimum Salary USD $100,000.00/Yr. Maximum Salary USD $120,000.00/Yr. Options Create Profile & Apply Apply Share Email this job to a friend Refer Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com"
    },
    "https://careers-nyit.icims.com/jobs/4282/assistant-associate-professor%2c-clinical-sciences/job": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor, Clinical Sciences",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor, Clinical Sciences Job Location(s) US-NY-Old Westbury Posted Date 2 months ago (8/17/2026 1:11 PM) Job ID 2026-4685 Division Clinical Sciences Position Type Part Time Faculty Type Regular Part-Time Category College of Osteopathic Medicine Overview New York Institute of Technology's six schools and colleges offer undergraduate, graduate, doctoral, and professional degree programs in in-demand disciplines including computer science, data science, and cybersecurity; biology, health professions, and medicine; architecture and design; engineering; IT and digital technologies; management; and energy and sustainability. A nonprofit, independent, private, and nonsectarian institute of higher education founded in 1955, it welcomes nearly 8,000 students worldwide. The university has campuses in New York City and Long Island, New York; Jonesboro, Arkansas; and Vancouver, British Columbia, as well as programs around the world. More than 120,000 alumni are part of an engaged network of physicians, architects, scientists, engineers, business leaders, digital artists, and healthcare professionals. Together, the university’s community of doers, makers, healers, and innovators empowers graduates to change the world, solve 21st-century challenges, and reinvent the future. For more information, visit nyit.edu . NYTech, College of Osteopathic Medicine, seeks an Assistant or Associate Professor, part time, located at the Old Westbury campus. Teaching assignments may be scheduled on Wednesdays, Thursdays, or a combination of both days, based on departmental needs for 38 weeks. Responsibilities Participate in teaching students in Osteopathic Manipulative Medicine program of NYITCOM at Old Westbury. Support the Department of Osteopathic Manipulative Medicine and its activities to include pre-clinical and clinical teaching. Serving as an instructor/table trainer in the OMM Lab. Grading students on OMM practical examinations. Other duties assigned for the department and/or college as the need arise. Qualifications D.O. or M.D. degree from a COCA or LCME approved school of osteopathic medicine or medicine. Board Certified or Board Eligible Other Information New York Institute of Technology is an Equal Opportunity Employer – All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. In compliance with local legislation as well as to provide greater transparency to candidates, the annual base salary range for this position is listed. New York Tech considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate experience/expertise, education/training, key skills, geographic location, internal peer equity as well as market, organizational considerations and/or applicable collective bargaining agreement when extending an offer. Minimum Salary USD $40,000.00/Yr. Maximum Salary USD $40,000.00/Yr. Options Create Profile & Apply Apply Share Email this job to a friend Refer Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com"
