    "https://careers-nyit.icims.com/jobs/4276/adjunct-faculty---chemistry/job": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Chemistry",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Chemistry Job Location(s) US-NY-Old Westbury Posted Date 2 months ago (8/11/2026 1:08 PM) Job ID 2026-4663 Division College of Arts & Sciences Position Type Adjunct Type Adjunct Category College of Arts and Sciences Overview New York Institute of Technology's six schools and colleges offer undergraduate, graduate, doctoral, and professional degree programs in in-demand disciplines including computer science, data science, and cybersecurity; biology, health professions, and medicine; architecture and design; engineering; IT and digital technologies; management; and energy and sustainability. A nonprofit, independent, private, and nonsectarian institute of higher education founded in 1955, it welcomes nearly 8,000 students worldwide. The university has campuses in New York City and Long Island, New York; Jonesboro, Arkansas; and Vancouver, British Columbia, as well as programs around the world. More than 120,000 alumni are part of an engaged network of physicians, architects, scientists, engineers, business leaders, digital artists, and healthcare professionals. Together, the university’s community of doers, makers, healers, and innovators empowers graduates to change the world, solve 21st-century challenges, and reinvent the future. For more information, visit nyit.edu . Responsibilities The Department of Biological and Chemical Sciences at New York Institute of Technology invites applications for an adjunct professor of Chemistry to teach general and chemistry courses on the Old Westbury campus. To apply for a position, please include the following attachments in your application package: a cover letter indicating which position you are interested in, a resume/CV, contact information for three (3) professional references, and a transcript (unofficial is fine) of your highest completed degree. Incomplete packages will not be reviewed. Qualifications Candidates must possess Ph.D. in Chemistry or related field. Undergraduate teaching experience is preferred. New York Institute of Technology emphasizes interdisciplinary scholarship, research, and teaching. Other Information New York Institute of Technology is an Equal Opportunity Employer – All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. In compliance with local legislation as well as to provide greater transparency to candidates, the annual base salary range for this position is listed. New York Tech considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate experience/expertise, education/training, key skills, geographic location, internal peer equity as well as market, organizational considerations and/or applicable collective bargaining agreement when extending an offer. Adjunct Faculty offered hourly rate is contingent on applicable rank. Minimum Salary USD $101.00/Hr. Maximum Salary USD $110.00/Hr. Options Create Profile & Apply Apply Share Email this job to a friend Refer Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com"
    },
    "https://careers-nyit.icims.com/jobs/4275/assistant-teaching-professor-in-physics/job": {
      "title": "Assistant Teaching Professor in Physics",
      "description": "Assistant Teaching Professor in Physics Job Location(s) US-NY-New York Posted Date 3 months ago (8/4/2026 8:48 AM) Job ID 2026-4665 Division College of Arts & Sciences Position Type Faculty Type Regular Full-Time Category Education Overview New York Institute of Technology's six schools and colleges offer undergraduate, graduate, doctoral, and professional degree programs in in-demand disciplines including computer science, data science, and cybersecurity; biology, health professions, and medicine; architecture and design; engineering; IT and digital technologies; management; and energy and sustainability. A nonprofit, independent, private, and nonsectarian institute of higher education founded in 1955, it welcomes nearly 8,000 students worldwide. The university has campuses in New York City and Long Island, New York; Jonesboro, Arkansas; and Vancouver, British Columbia, as well as programs around the world. More than 120,000 alumni are part of an engaged network of physicians, architects, scientists, engineers, business leaders, digital artists, and healthcare professionals. Together, the university’s community of doers, makers, healers, and innovators empowers graduates to change the world, solve 21st-century challenges, and reinvent the future. For more information, visit nyit.edu . The Department of Physics invites applications for a full-time Assistant Teaching Professor position at NYIT’s New York City Campus. As our student body and institution evolve, we seek a forward-thinking educator who will teach creatively and grow alongside our department . Responsibilities The successful candidate will (1) teach engaging, interactive physics courses for majors, minors, and non-majors, (2) modernize and develop course materials in existing courses, (3) create new courses and curricula tailored to changing student needs, (4) contribute to the NYIT community through service activities such as student academic advising and mentoring, recruitment initiatives, and department- college- and school-wide committees. The teaching load for the position is 21 credit hours per year. The initial appointment will be for two years, with subsequent reappointments (subject to approval by the university) for two consecutive three-year contracts, followed by renewable five-year contracts with possibility of promotion to Associate Teaching Professor and Teaching Professor. Qualifications Required Qualifications: Ph.D. in Physics or a closely related field by the time of appointment. Demonstrated success in undergraduate teaching and a commitment to educating students from different backgrounds. Preferred qualifications: Experience creating and teaching advanced undergraduate laboratory courses. Experience and future plans for meaningfully involving undergraduate students in physics research. Expected start date: Jan 2027 or Sept 2027 depending on candidate availability Deadline for applications: open until filled, with review of applications to begin Sept 28, 2026 Application materials candidates should include: Applicants should submit the following materials as a single PDF under the CV section. Additional information may be uploaded in the additional details tabs. Cover Letter addressing how your skills align with our department's and student needs. Curriculum Vitae (CV). Teaching Statement (1–2 pages) detailing teaching philosophy and experience. Contact Information for three professional references. Student and Peer Teaching Evaluation forms from previous teaching experience are preferred but not required. Other Information New York Institute of Technology offers numerous opportunities to enhance personal and professional growth and provides employees with a competitive compensation and benefits program inclusive of generous paid time off, holidays, tuition remission, and retirement plans with employer contributions. New York Institute of Technology is an Equal Opportunity Employer – All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. In compliance with local legislation as well as to provide greater transparency to candidates, the annual base salary range for this position is listed. New York Tech considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate experience/expertise, education/training, key skills, geographic location, internal peer equity as well as market, organizational considerations and/or applicable collective bargaining agreement when extending an offer. Minimum Salary USD $75,000.00/Yr. Maximum Salary USD $85,000.00/Yr. Options Create Profile & Apply Apply Share Email this job to a friend Refer Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com"
    },
    "https://careers-nyit.icims.com/jobs/4274/teaching-assistant-professor-of-mathematics/job": {
      "title": "Teaching Assistant Professor of Mathematics",
      "description": "Teaching Assistant Professor of Mathematics Job Location(s) US-NY-New York Posted Date 2 months ago (8/5/2026 6:39 PM) Job ID 2026-4664 Division College of Arts & Sciences Position Type Faculty Type Regular Full-Time Category Education Overview NY Tech’s College of Arts and Sciences seeks a full-time Teaching Assistant Professor, Mathematics, located at the New York City campus. Responsibilities The successful candidate is required to teach 21 credit hours during the academic year. Assigned courses include all pre-calculus and calculus service courses, as well as other advanced courses within the candidate's area of specialization. Additional responsibilities include participation in curriculum development and service to the Mathematics Department, including initiatives to reform pre-calculus and calculus courses through the implementation of active learning strategies designed to improve student retention and success. Qualifications A doctoral degree in Mathematics Education / Mathematics / Applied Mathematics / Statistics from a Mathematics Department is required. Preference will be given to candidates having prior teaching experience at a university. Additionally, we are seeking candidates with experience increasing student engagement in pre-calculus courses using active learning methods, with experience in the development of teaching materials that promote active learning, and who can assist with the professional development of pre-calculus instructors. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled with a start date of as early as Jan. 25, 2027, but a start date of Sept. 2027 is also possible. Please submit cover letter, resume, statement of teaching, any scholarly interests and a list of references for consideration. Review of applications will continue until the position is filled. New York Institute of Technology's six schools and colleges offer undergraduate, graduate, doctoral, and professional degree programs in in-demand disciplines including computer science, data science, and cybersecurity; biology, health professions, and medicine; architecture and design; engineering; IT and digital technologies; management; and energy and sustainability. A nonprofit, independent, private, and nonsectarian institute of higher education founded in 1955, it welcomes nearly 8,000 students worldwide. The university has campuses in New York City and Long Island, New York; Jonesboro, Arkansas; and Vancouver, British Columbia, as well as programs around the world. More than 120,000 alumni are part of an engaged network of physicians, architects, scientists, engineers, business leaders, digital artists, and healthcare professionals. Together, the university’s community of doers, makers, healers, and innovators empowers graduates to change the world, solve 21st-century challenges, and reinvent the future. For more information, visit nyit.edu . Other Information New York Institute of Technology offers numerous opportunities to enhance personal and professional growth and provides employees with a competitive compensation and benefits program inclusive of generous paid time off, holidays, tuition remission, and retirement plans with employer contributions. New York Institute of Technology is an Equal Opportunity Employer – All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. In compliance with local legislation as well as to provide greater transparency to candidates, the annual base salary range for this position is listed. New York Tech considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate experience/expertise, education/training, key skills, geographic location, internal peer equity as well as market, organizational considerations and/or applicable collective bargaining agreement when extending an offer. Minimum Salary USD $75,000.00/Yr. Maximum Salary USD $85,000.00/Yr. Options Create Profile & Apply Apply Share Email this job to a friend Refer Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com"
