    "https://careers-nyit.icims.com/jobs/4254/adjunct-faculty--marketing-%26-management/job": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty- Marketing & Management",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty- Marketing & Management Job Location(s) US-NY-New York Posted Date 4 months ago (6/29/2026 3:18 PM) Job ID 2026-4595 Division School of Management Position Type Adjunct Type Adjunct Category School of Management Overview New York Institute of Technology's six schools and colleges offer undergraduate, graduate, doctoral, and professional degree programs in in-demand disciplines including computer science, data science, and cybersecurity; biology, health professions, and medicine; architecture and design; engineering; IT and digital technologies; management; and energy and sustainability. A nonprofit, independent, private, and nonsectarian institute of higher education founded in 1955, it welcomes nearly 8,000 students worldwide. The university has campuses in New York City and Long Island, New York; Jonesboro, Arkansas; and Vancouver, British Columbia, as well as programs around the world. More than 120,000 alumni are part of an engaged network of physicians, architects, scientists, engineers, business leaders, digital artists, and healthcare professionals. Together, the university’s community of doers, makers, healers, and innovators empowers graduates to change the world, solve 21st-century challenges, and reinvent the future. For more information, visit nyit.edu . Responsibilities The School of Management at New York Institute of Technology is looking for Adjunct Faculty to teach a Cyber Law, Policy and Ethics course, in-person, at the undergraduate and/or graduate level at its New York City campus in the Fall of 2026. Teach a Cyber Law, Policy and Ethics course, in-person in alignment with program goals and institutional standards. Develop and deliver engaging lectures, class discussions, case studies, and relevant assignments that align with course objectives and learning outcomes. Provide timely, constructive feedback and academic guidance to support student learning, engagement, and skill development. Create, administer, and grade assessments fairly and efficiently, including exams, quizzes, presentations, and projects. Utilize learning management systems (e.g., Canvas) for course delivery, communication, grading, and material sharing. Foster an inclusive and respectful learning environment that encourages participation, critical thinking, and professional growth. Be available to students during scheduled office hours or by appointment for academic advising, support, and mentorship. Collaborate with program directors and departmental faculty to continuously improve curriculum, assessments, and student learning outcomes. Ensure compliance with institutional policies, accreditation standards, and academic integrity guidelines. Attend and participate in faculty meetings, orientation sessions, training workshops, or department planning as required. Engage in professional development to stay current in the higher education instruction. Support assessment and accreditation activities by maintaining accurate records and submitting required reports or materials Qualifications To be considered for the position, candidates need to have a law degree (J.D.) and 5 years of professional experience in the fields of cyber law, financial crimes, and compliance law. Prior teaching experience is desirable but not required. Admission to the New York State Bar is a plus, as well as applied data science knowledge. Candidates must be available to teach on-campus, day and/or evenings. Other Information New York Institute of Technology is an Equal Opportunity Employer – All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. In compliance with local legislation as well as to provide greater transparency to candidates, the annual base salary range for this position is listed. New York Tech considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate experience/expertise, education/training, key skills, geographic location, internal peer equity as well as market, organizational considerations and/or applicable collective bargaining agreement when extending an offer. Adjunct Faculty offered hourly rate is contingent on applicable rank. Minimum Salary USD $101.00/Hr. Maximum Salary USD $110.00/Hr. Options Create Profile & Apply Apply Share Email this job to a friend Refer Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com"
    },
    "https://careers-nyit.icims.com/jobs/4253/digital-technology-specialist/job": {
      "title": "Digital Technology Specialist",
      "description": "Digital Technology Specialist Job Location(s) US-NY-New York | US-NY-Old Westbury Posted Date 4 months ago (6/29/2026 3:09 PM) Job ID 2026-4598 Division School of Architecture & Design Position Type Staff Type Regular Full-Time Category Education Overview New York Institute of Technology's six schools and colleges offer undergraduate, graduate, doctoral, and professional degree programs in in-demand disciplines including computer science, data science, and cybersecurity; biology, health professions, and medicine; architecture and design; engineering; IT and digital technologies; management; and energy and sustainability. A nonprofit, independent, private, and nonsectarian institute of higher education founded in 1955, it welcomes nearly 8,000 students worldwide. The university has campuses in New York City and Long Island, New York; Jonesboro, Arkansas; and Vancouver, British Columbia, as well as programs around the world. More than 120,000 alumni are part of an engaged network of physicians, architects, scientists, engineers, business leaders, digital artists, and healthcare professionals. Together, the university’s community of doers, makers, healers, and innovators empowers graduates to change the world, solve 21st-century challenges, and reinvent the future. For more information, visit nyit.edu . The School of Architecture and Design (SOAD) invites applications for the position of Digital Technology Specialist. Based primarily on the Long Island (Old Westbury) campus, with periodic travel to the Manhattan campus, this position supports the school's growing ecosystem of digital fabrication, computational design, robotics, physical computing, artificial intelligence, immersive technologies, and emerging design technologies. Reporting to the Director of Digital Technology and Fabrication, the Digital Technology Specialist will serve as a key technical and educational resource for students, faculty, and staff. The successful candidate will help advance innovative research, teaching, and creative practice through expertise in digital fabrication, computational workflows, robotics, electronics, and emerging design technologies. Responsibilities Serve as a primary technical specialist within NYIT's digital fabrication laboratories, supporting teaching, research, and interdisciplinary projects. Operate, maintain, troubleshoot, and improve digital fabrication systems including CNC milling, laser cutting, additive manufacturing, robotic fabrication, scanning technologies, and related equipment. Support computational design workflows with particular emphasis on Rhino and Grasshopper, including parametric modeling, digital-to-physical fabrication, robotic control, simulation, and data-driven design processes. Assist students and faculty with projects involving robotics, Arduino, sensors, embedded electronics, physical computing, interactive installations, and other emerging technologies. Qualifications Required Qualifications : Bachelor’s degree in architecture, Design, Engineering, Digital Fabrication, Computational Design, or a related field. Demonstrated experience in digital fabrication, design technology, or related professional and/or academic environments. Advanced proficiency with Rhino and Grasshopper. Experience operating and supporting multiple fabrication technologies such as CNC milling, laser cutting, 3D printing, robotic systems, scanning technologies, or related equipment. Strong problem-solving, organizational, communication, and technical troubleshooting skills. Ability to support students and faculty from concept development through fabrication and implementation. Ability to lift equipment and materials and work in an active fabrication environment. Flexibility to occasionally work evenings and weekends in support of academic programming. Preferred Qualifications: Master's degree in a related field. Experience with CAD/CAM workflows (RhinoCAM) and digital fabrication software. Experience with robotic fabrication systems and automation workflows. Experience with Arduino, Raspberry Pi, sensors, actuators, and physical computing systems. Experience with AI-enabled design workflows, machine vision, reality capture, AR/VR/XR technologies, or interactive environments. Experience teaching workshops, supporting research initiatives, or working within higher education environments. Required Application Materials: 1. Cover Letter 2. Resume/CV 3. Portfolio (PDF) demonstrating relevant work in digital fabrication, computational design, robotics, physical computing, research, and related areas. 4. Contact information for three professional references. Other Information New York Institute of Technology offers numerous opportunities to enhance personal and professional growth and provides employees with a competitive compensation and benefits program inclusive of generous paid time off, holidays, tuition remission, and retirement plans with employer contributions. New York Institute of Technology is an Equal Opportunity Employer – All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. In compliance with local legislation as well as to provide greater transparency to candidates, the annual base salary range for this position is listed. New York Tech considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate experience/expertise, education/training, key skills, geographic location, internal peer equity as well as market, organizational considerations and/or applicable collective bargaining agreement when extending an offer. Minimum Salary USD $65,000.00/Yr. Maximum Salary USD $75,000.00/Yr. Options Create Profile & Apply Apply Share Email this job to a friend Refer Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com"
    },
    "https://careers-nyit.icims.com/jobs/4251/associate-director%2c-pipeline-programs/job": {
      "title": "Associate Director, Pipeline Programs",
      "description": "Associate Director, Pipeline Programs Job Location(s) US-AR-Jonesboro Posted Date 3 months ago (7/22/2026 5:03 PM) Job ID 2026-4563 Division Admissions Position Type Staff Type Regular Full-Time Category Enrollment - Admissions Overview New York Institute of Technology's six schools and colleges offer undergraduate, graduate, doctoral, and professional degree programs in in-demand disciplines including computer science, data science, and cybersecurity; biology, health professions, and medicine; architecture and design; engineering; IT and digital technologies; management; and energy and sustainability. A nonprofit, independent, private, and nonsectarian institute of higher education founded in 1955, it welcomes nearly 8,000 students worldwide. The university has campuses in New York City and Long Island, New York; Jonesboro, Arkansas; and Vancouver, British Columbia, as well as programs around the world. More than 120,000 alumni are part of an engaged network of physicians, architects, scientists, engineers, business leaders, digital artists, and healthcare professionals. Together, the university’s community of doers, makers, healers, and innovators empowers graduates to change the world, solve 21st-century challenges, and reinvent the future. For more information, visit nyit.edu . NYTech’s College of Osteopathic Medicine seeks an Associate Director Pipeline Programs located at the Jonesboro, Arkansas campus. The Associate Director for Pipeline Programs will develop, organize and coordinate activities to build a strong pipeline for incoming first year medical students to NYITCOM at Arkansas State University. The programs developed will meet prospective student needs; build relationships with key secondary and postsecondary school personnel; work with the COM's faculty and staff to enhance outreach efforts to prospective students, particularly to those in under-represented and economically disadvantaged groups; conduct strategy meetings for calendar and program development; develop, organize, and coordinate a Peer Outreach Mentor Program; attend program meetings; perform recruitment, retention and tracking activities; serve on committees and work groups as requested; refer students to appropriate staff/faculty/program for support; develop working relationships with targeted schools; coordinate with Student Administration and Academic Affairs staff to create a pathway to the pre-matriculation and other support programs; develop outreach activities to local high schools with Peer Outreach Mentors; The ADPP will also serve as part of the Student Administration team. Responsibilities Conduct extensive research in Arkansas and designated surrounding states to assess the needs of under-represented and economically disadvantaged student populations in K-12 and pre-med programs to prepare them for future college and careers. Create, develop and execute on- and off-campus pipeline programs to meet the needs of prospective students, including, but not limited to, workshops, leadership development, tours, professional development, science and math prep courses, cultural events and activities, and support and training on applying to medical school. Develop, cultivate and maintain relationships with key individuals, groups and institutions (school district superintendents, school level administrators and faculty, pre-med advisors, BS/DO and Pathway programs coordinators, AACOM representatives, NAAHP/SAAHP representatives) to recruit K-12 and pre-med candidates for the medical school or other STEM professions. Create, implement and maintain an assessment program for the recruitment, retention, and tracking of pipeline program outcomes and participants. Aid/Attend strategic recruitment events to enhance NYITCOM student recruitment efforts and programming. Collaborate with admissions staff to invoke pipeline/pathway conversations with key stakeholders and undergraduate/graduate students Develop and maintain partnerships with key NYITCOM staff and faculty. Organize and manage the Outreach Mentor Program and Student Ambassador Education Team, developing outreach and education opportunities for the student doctors, coordinating with the Director of Community Outreach and/or Director of Admissions. Research and identify federal, state and private funding sources for student preparation programs. Train and supervise student assistants and others as assigned. Qualifications A Bachelor’s Degree is required. Experience in program development and implementation is. required. Community development and program outreach preferred. Able to initiate, develop and manage multiple projects and programs independently and simultaneously; must be able to work independently. Flexible and adaptable to change; must have ability to travel and work evenings and weekends. Strong organizational and decision-making skills; able to play either a leading or supporting role. Must be able to appreciate and understand culturally and internationally diverse student population; knowledge of international educational credentials needed. Proficient in use of all computer programs. Other Information New York Institute of Technology offers numerous opportunities to enhance personal and professional growth and provides employees with a competitive compensation and benefits program inclusive of generous paid time off, holidays, and retirement plans with employer contributions. New York Institute of Technology is an Equal Opportunity Employer – All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. Options Create Profile & Apply Apply Share Email this job to a friend Refer Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com"
    },
