    "https://careers-nyit.icims.com/jobs/4246/adjunct-faculty---physician-assistant-studies/job": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Physician Assistant Studies",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Physician Assistant Studies Job Location(s) US-NY-Old Westbury Posted Date 4 months ago (6/25/2026 6:11 PM) Job ID 2026-4594 Division School of Health Professions Position Type Adjunct Type Adjunct Category School of Health Professions Overview New York Institute of Technology's six schools and colleges offer undergraduate, graduate, doctoral, and professional degree programs in in-demand disciplines including computer science, data science, and cybersecurity; biology, health professions, and medicine; architecture and design; engineering; IT and digital technologies; management; and energy and sustainability. A nonprofit, independent, private, and nonsectarian institute of higher education founded in 1955, it welcomes nearly 8,000 students worldwide. The university has campuses in New York City and Long Island, New York; Jonesboro, Arkansas; and Vancouver, British Columbia, as well as programs around the world. More than 120,000 alumni are part of an engaged network of physicians, architects, scientists, engineers, business leaders, digital artists, and healthcare professionals. Together, the university’s community of doers, makers, healers, and innovators empowers graduates to change the world, solve 21st-century challenges, and reinvent the future. For more information, visit nyit.edu . Responsibilities The Department of Physician Assistant Studies at New York Institute of Technology (NYIT) seeks dynamic, experienced, and student-centered adjunct faculty to join our team. Adjunct faculty will teach in the didactic or clinical phase of the Master of Science in Physician Assistant Studies program, depending on area of expertise. This role includes in-person instruction, student assessment, and collaboration with full-time faculty to deliver high-quality, competency-based medical education. Reporting to the Program Director, adjunct faculty serve as content experts, educators, and professional role models who support student learning and academic success. Deliver assigned lectures or lab instruction in accordance with the course syllabus and program goals Integrate varied instructional methodologies to foster active learning and student engagement Utilize NYIT’s Learning Management System (Canvas) to support course delivery and communication Assess student performance through exams, assignments, and/or observed competencies Provide timely remediation and feedback to students in accordance with department policies Contribute to course and program-level assessment and quality improvement processes Maintain accurate records of attendance and grades Uphold academic integrity and ensure a supportive, inclusive learning environment Collaborate with course directors or the Director of Didactic Education on course materials and improvements Attend scheduled course-related meetings as requested by the course director or program administration. Adhere to program policies, including academic integrity, assessment protocols, and grading timelines. Hold office hours to meet with students outside of class to support learning Qualifications Terminal degree or graduate degree in a field relevant to the assigned course content (e.g., MS, PhD, MD, DO, PA-C, PharmD, or another applicable credential). Current board certification and licensure, if applicable, in the healthcare profession aligned with course content. Minimum of three years of clinical or academic experience in the subject area being taught. Excellent communication, organizational, and interpersonal skills. Preferred Qualifications: Prior teaching or instructional experience in higher education preferred. Familiarity with ARC-PA accreditation standards Experience using instructional technologies Other Information New York Institute of Technology is an Equal Opportunity Employer – All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. In compliance with local legislation as well as to provide greater transparency to candidates, the annual base salary range for this position is listed. New York Tech considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate experience/expertise, education/training, key skills, geographic location, internal peer equity as well as market, organizational considerations and/or applicable collective bargaining agreement when extending an offer. Adjunct Faculty offered hourly rate is contingent on applicable rank. Minimum Salary USD $101.00/Hr. Maximum Salary USD $110.00/Hr. Options Create Profile & Apply Apply Share Email this job to a friend Refer Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com"
    },
    "https://careers-nyit.icims.com/jobs/4244/associate-director%2c-counseling-and-wellness-services/job": {
      "title": "Associate Director, Counseling and Wellness Services",
      "description": "Associate Director, Counseling and Wellness Services Job Location(s) US-NY-Old Westbury Posted Date 4 months ago (6/29/2026 4:17 PM) Job ID 2026-4590 Division College of Osteopathic Medicine Position Type Staff Type Regular Full-Time Category Student Life Work Mode Hybrid Overview New York Institute of Technology's six schools and colleges offer undergraduate, graduate, doctoral, and professional degree programs in in-demand disciplines including computer science, data science, and cybersecurity; biology, health professions, and medicine; architecture and design; engineering; IT and digital technologies; management; and energy and sustainability. A nonprofit, independent, private, and nonsectarian institute of higher education founded in 1955, it welcomes nearly 8,000 students worldwide. The university has campuses in New York City and Long Island, New York; Jonesboro, Arkansas; and Vancouver, British Columbia, as well as programs around the world. More than 120,000 alumni are part of an engaged network of physicians, architects, scientists, engineers, business leaders, digital artists, and healthcare professionals. Together, the university’s community of doers, makers, healers, and innovators empowers graduates to change the world, solve 21st-century challenges, and reinvent the future. For more information, visit nyit.edu . Responsibilities Primary role is to administer intake assessments and provide individual/group mental health counseling to medical students (which may include, identifying and managing personal issues that might affect their academic performance and interfere with their ability to focus on coursework, meet deadlines, or prepare adequately for exams.) Provide crisis intervention, triage appointments, and short-term therapy, as needed. This also includes hospitalizations and, at times, on call responsibilities. Maintain timely department documentation (progress notes, case management notes, monthly statistics, etc.) Contribute and assist the NYITCOM Director of Counseling and Wellness and Associate Director of Counseling and Wellness in planning and implementing programs, workshops, and events related to mental health topics and other topics of interest to medical students. Assist in outreach, promoting department programs, and sharing mental health and wellbeing information (via Instagram posts, creating fliers, displaying materials on department bulletin boards) Provide support and resources for faculty and staff regarding medical students of concern. Support Director of NYITCOM Counseling and Wellness in implementing counseling and wellness policies and procedures at the NYITCOM. Assist at NYITCOM Events (Orientations, White Coat Ceremony, Commencement Ceremony, etc.) Qualifications Master’s Degree in Social Work or Mental Health Counseling is required Required field of expertise in Counseling Required Licensure(s): New York state Licensure in Mental Health Counseling (LMHC) or in Social Work (LCSW) is required 3 to 5 years directly related experience or five to eight years’ related experience Familiarity with therapy models and approaches that are appropriate for addressing a wide range of mental health concerns Excellent interpersonal, computer/technological (Microsoft Office products, electronic health record, and social media platforms ), organizational, oral and written communication skills. Demonstrate cultural competence and the ability to work with faculty, staff, and students from a wide range of diverse backgrounds. Must be available to work with a flexible schedule of day and evening hours Must be detailed oriented, self-motivated and able to work independently Other Information New York Institute of Technology offers numerous opportunities to enhance personal and professional growth and provides employees with a competitive compensation and benefits program inclusive of generous paid time off, holidays, tuition remission, and retirement plans with employer contributions. New York Institute of Technology is an Equal Opportunity Employer – All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. In compliance with local legislation as well as to provide greater transparency to candidates, the annual base salary range for this position is listed. New York Tech considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate experience/expertise, education/training, key skills, geographic location, internal peer equity as well as market, organizational considerations and/or applicable collective bargaining agreement when extending an offer. Minimum Salary USD $70,000.00/Yr. Maximum Salary USD $75,000.00/Yr. Options Create Profile & Apply Apply Share Email this job to a friend Refer Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com"
    },
    "https://careers-nyit.icims.com/jobs/4239/administrative-specialist/job": {
      "title": "Administrative Specialist",
      "description": "Administrative Specialist Job Location(s) US-NY-Old Westbury Posted Date 4 months ago (7/1/2026 9:41 AM) Job ID 2026-4579 Division College of Osteopathic Medicine Position Type Staff Type Regular Full-Time Category Administrative/Clerical Overview New York Institute of Technology's six schools and colleges offer undergraduate, graduate, doctoral, and professional degree programs in in-demand disciplines including computer science, data science, and cybersecurity; biology, health professions, and medicine; architecture and design; engineering; IT and digital technologies; management; and energy and sustainability. A nonprofit, independent, private, and nonsectarian institute of higher education founded in 1955, it welcomes nearly 8,000 students worldwide. The university has campuses in New York City and Long Island, New York; Jonesboro, Arkansas; and Vancouver, British Columbia, as well as programs around the world. More than 120,000 alumni are part of an engaged network of physicians, architects, scientists, engineers, business leaders, digital artists, and healthcare professionals. Together, the university’s community of doers, makers, healers, and innovators empowers graduates to change the world, solve 21st-century challenges, and reinvent the future. For more information, visit nyit.edu . NYTech’s College of Osteopathic Medicine seeks an Administrative Specialist for the department of Osteopathic and Manipulative Medicine (OMM) located at the Long island (Old Westbury, NY) campus. Responsibilities Provide administrative support to the faculty and the Department of Osteopathic Manipulative Medicine (OMM) to ensure efficient daily operations and support of departmental, academic, clinical, and event-related activities. Assist faculty with departmental and school-related needs, including ordering supplies, scrubs, and equipment, and supporting faculty requests related to technology, logistics, and general administrative operations. Track faculty attendance and manage vacation and absence requests. Coordinate and submit clinic block schedules and assist with faculty scheduling needs. Facilitate and support work-study students and the OMM Teaching Assistant (TA) program, including scheduling, communication, and administrative coordination. Maintain and manage the department’s teaching, clinic, and event calendars, including scheduling and reservations for the OMM laboratory and other campus spaces. Manage calendar and schedules, ensuring efficient coordination of meetings, appointments, and events while maintaining strong organization and attention to detail. Process, monitor, and track departmental expenditures, faculty reimbursements, purchasing requests, and event-related expenses. Assist with budget oversight and financial administrative processes, including Workday transactions, purchasing workflows, and expense tracking. Budget management. Assist with planning and coordinating departmental meetings, continuing medical education (CME) events, and OMM Center programming, including identifying appropriate event space, managing registration, ordering catering, requesting ATG and facilities support, and coordinating logistics for successful event execution. Support promotional and communication efforts for departmental and OMM Center events, including advertising, announcements, and outreach to faculty, staff, students, and external participants. Assist with coordinating and scheduling student organization activities (including SAAO events), as well as scheduling student rotations with OMM department faculty. Serve as a primary departmental liaison for students, faculty, research subjects, and external inquiries, providing professional, timely, and responsive communication. Maintain accurate records, support departmental reporting needs, and ensure administrative processes are handled in a timely and organized manner. Other duties as assigned to support the department and college as needs arise. Qualifications A Bachelor of Arts degree is required or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Familiarity with budget management and Workday systems is highly prefered. Proficiency in MS office, Adobe Suites, Zoom, Microsoft Teams. Strong organizational skills with the ability to multi-task. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Attention to detail and problem solving skills. Excellent time management skills and the ability to prioritize work Other Information New York Institute of Technology offers numerous opportunities to enhance personal and professional growth and provides employees with a competitive compensation and benefits program inclusive of generous paid time off, holidays, tuition remission, and retirement plans with employer contributions. New York Institute of Technology is an Equal Opportunity Employer – All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. In compliance with local legislation as well as to provide greater transparency to candidates, the annual base salary range for this position is listed. New York Tech considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate experience/expertise, education/training, key skills, geographic location, internal peer equity as well as market, organizational considerations and/or applicable collective bargaining agreement when extending an offer. Minimum Salary USD $50,000.00/Yr. Maximum Salary USD $55,000.00/Yr. Options Create Profile & Apply Apply Share Email this job to a friend Refer Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com"
    },
    "https://careers-nyit.icims.com/jobs/4238/exam-proctor/job": {
      "title": "Exam Proctor",
      "description": "Exam Proctor Job Location(s) US-AR-Jonesboro Posted Date 4 months ago (6/29/2026 4:13 PM) Job ID 2026-4569 Division Academic Affairs Position Type Temporary Staff Type Temporary Part-Time Category Education Overview New York Institute of Technology's six schools and colleges offer undergraduate, graduate, doctoral, and professional degree programs in in-demand disciplines including computer science, data science, and cybersecurity; biology, health professions, and medicine; architecture and design; engineering; IT and digital technologies; management; and energy and sustainability. A nonprofit, independent, private, and nonsectarian institute of higher education founded in 1955, it welcomes nearly 8,000 students worldwide. The university has campuses in New York City and Long Island, New York; Jonesboro, Arkansas; and Vancouver, British Columbia, as well as programs around the world. More than 120,000 alumni are part of an engaged network of physicians, architects, scientists, engineers, business leaders, digital artists, and healthcare professionals. Together, the university’s community of doers, makers, healers, and innovators empowers graduates to change the world, solve 21st-century challenges, and reinvent the future. For more information, visit nyit.edu . Responsibilities The NYIT College of Osteopathic Medicine, Jonesboro campus seeks part-time/per-diem Exam Proctors to help with logistics during exams and monitor students while they take computer based exams. Proctors will help setup the exam room, check-in students, monitor them during the exam, and help with any exam related logistics. Selected candidates will be trained to perform these duties and will be supervised by NYIT staff. Oversee in-person and occasionally virtual examinations for NYIT College of Osteopathic Medicine as well as Master's in Biomedical Sciences students, including those requiring disability-related accommodations. Strictly enforce academic policies and exam specific regulations. Monitor students continuously throughout the testing period, provide seating/testing instructions, and manage the check-in and check-out processes. New proctors must obtain training from head/lead proctors and must attend NYITCOM’s Academic Affairs’ annual proctor meeting held at the beginning of each academic year. Qualifications Must be 18 years of age or older. High school diploma or higher is required. Ability to communicate clearly and effectively. Ability to work effectively on multiple tasks. Must be well organized. Must be computer efficient. Must be able to move quietly about the examination room(s). Must maintain professionalism and confidentiality at all times. Ability to enforce NYITCOM/NYIT policies for exams. Other Information New York Institute of Technology is an Equal Opportunity Employer – All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. Options Create Profile & Apply Apply Share Email this job to a friend Refer Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com"
    },
    "https://careers-nyit.icims.com/jobs/4237/standardized-patient/job": {
      "title": "Standardized Patient",
      "description": "Standardized Patient Job Location(s) US-AR-Jonesboro Posted Date 4 months ago (6/26/2026 10:14 AM) Job ID 2026-4571 Division College of Osteopathic Medicine Position Type Temporary Staff Type Temporary Part-Time Category College of Osteopathic Medicine Overview New York Institute of Technology's six schools and colleges offer undergraduate, graduate, doctoral, and professional degree programs in in-demand disciplines including computer science, data science, and cybersecurity; biology, health professions, and medicine; architecture and design; engineering; IT and digital technologies; management; and energy and sustainability. A nonprofit, independent, private, and nonsectarian institute of higher education founded in 1955, it welcomes nearly 8,000 students worldwide. The university has campuses in New York City and Long Island, New York; Jonesboro, Arkansas; and Vancouver, British Columbia, as well as programs around the world. More than 120,000 alumni are part of an engaged network of physicians, architects, scientists, engineers, business leaders, digital artists, and healthcare professionals. Together, the university’s community of doers, makers, healers, and innovators empowers graduates to change the world, solve 21st-century challenges, and reinvent the future. For more information, visit nyit.edu . Responsibilities New York Institute of Technology College of Osteopathic Medicine, Jonesboro, Arkansas campus seeks part time / by the day, week or case Standardized Patients (SPs). The Standardized Patient reports directly to the Standardized Patient Educator. The major responsibility of this position is to portray all of the characteristics of a real patient, simulating the signs and symptoms. Standardized Patients will often be physically examined (no invasive exams) by students and faculty as part of the medical students learning experience providing constructive feedback to medical students and colleagues. A standardized patient (SP) has the unique opportunity to shape the education of future physicians. By helping NYITCOM train our students, Standardized Patients will be a part of improving health care, and helping medical students to give empathetic care to all of their patients. This program is committed to diversity, equity, and inclusion, so application from underrepresented people groups is highly encouraged. Be highly dependable and punctual Demonstrate flexibility and reliability with scheduling and assignments. A typical assignment may be 20 – 30 hours in a week’s time, based on the specifics of the case. Must demonstrate the ability to be instructed by a Standardized Patient Educator and consistently simulate a case scenario in an accurate, reliable and professional manner. Provide constructive feedback to medical students and colleagues Be comfortable having repeated physical examination maneuvers (non-invasive) performed on self Be willing to wear a hospital gown with only undergarments underneath, while on camera and/or observed live through an observation window or video monitor Simulate all aspects of scenarios, including history of current problem, affect/behavior and physical findings, in a standardized, accurate, and reliable manner Accurately and consistently complete checklists Accept ongoing feedback from facilitators and incorporate into case simulation Be willing to be audio and videotaped during simulations Other duties as assigned. Work Schedule : Flexible Hours, day by day or week schedule based on case requirements. Must be flexible regarding scheduling and assignments, as needed. We offer competitive wages and flexible schedules. Paid training is provided to all Standardized Patients. Interviews take place periodically during the year. Working as a Standardized Patient is considered an hourly temporary job. The hours will depend on the needs of the events throughout the year. Qualifications High School diploma or equivalent is required. Ability to follow directions and communicate both written and verbally. Strong reading and writing skills to absorb and use the detailed case training and exam procedural information. Must have excellent recall of learner performance. Attention to detail is essential. Must have a solid internet connection and intermediate computer skills for training and scheduling. Other Information New York Institute of Technology is an Equal Opportunity Employer – All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. Options Create Profile & Apply Apply Share Email this job to a friend Refer Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com"
    },
    "https://careers-nyit.icims.com/jobs/4236/clinic-nurse%2c-prn/job": {
      "title": "Clinic Nurse, PRN",
      "description": "Clinic Nurse, PRN Job Location(s) US-AR-Jonesboro Posted Date 4 months ago (6/18/2026 10:37 AM) Job ID 2026-4570 Division College of Osteopathic Medicine Position Type Temporary Staff Type Temporary Part-Time Category College of Osteopathic Medicine Overview New York Institute of Technology's six schools and colleges offer undergraduate, graduate, doctoral, and professional degree programs in in-demand disciplines including computer science, data science, and cybersecurity; biology, health professions, and medicine; architecture and design; engineering; IT and digital technologies; management; and energy and sustainability. A nonprofit, independent, private, and nonsectarian institute of higher education founded in 1955, it welcomes nearly 8,000 students worldwide. The university has campuses in New York City and Long Island, New York; Jonesboro, Arkansas; and Vancouver, British Columbia, as well as programs around the world. More than 120,000 alumni are part of an engaged network of physicians, architects, scientists, engineers, business leaders, digital artists, and healthcare professionals. Together, the university’s community of doers, makers, healers, and innovators empowers graduates to change the world, solve 21st-century challenges, and reinvent the future. For more information, visit nyit.edu . Responsibilities Collecting medical histories and monitoring vital signs, documenting in the EMR Assisting physicians with minor in-office surgical procedures and physical examinations Performing routine screenings such as hearing, vision, ECG, etc. Administering medications, injections, immunizations and performing wound care or dressing changes Assessing patient needs via phone or in person; coordinating care with other specialist, facilitating follow up, responding to messages from physicians Adhering to infection control protocols and maintaining a clean, safe workplace and equipment Restocking rooms, routine autoclave cleaning of equipment Qualifications LPN or RN degree required. Ability to manage high patient volumes in an efficient manner. Strong interpersonal skills for patient, family and team communication. Proficiency in technical nursing skills such as IV start, blood draws, dressings, manual vitals. Other Information New York Institute of Technology is an Equal Opportunity Employer – All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. Options Create Profile & Apply Apply Share Email this job to a friend Refer Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com"
